(window.STEP_BOOK = window.STEP_BOOK || {})["C2"] = {"n":2,"level":"A2","t":"Building Better Paragraphs","lessons":[{"id":"2.1","t":"The Topic Sentence","html":"<p><strong>Unit 2 · Lesson 2.1 · CEFR A2 · STEP link: Composition Analysis (10%)</strong></p>\n<h3>Objectives</h3>\n<p>1. Identify and write a clear topic sentence.</p>\n<p>2. Choose the best topic sentence for a paragraph.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الأهداف</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">١. أن يتعرف الطالب على جملة الموضوع الواضحة ويكتبها.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٢. أن يختار أفضل جملة موضوع لفقرة.</span></p>\n<h3>The Skill</h3>\n<p>The topic sentence is usually the FIRST sentence of a paragraph. It has two parts: the TOPIC (what the paragraph is about) and the CONTROLLING IDEA (what the writer wants to say about the topic). In 'Cycling is a great way to travel around the city', the topic is cycling and the controlling idea is a great way to travel.</p>\n<p>A good topic sentence is neither too narrow nor too broad. Too narrow: it gives only one detail (My bike is blue), so it cannot cover the other sentences. Too broad: it is so general that it could open a hundred different paragraphs (Sports are fun). The best topic sentence fits ALL the supporting sentences exactly.</p>\n<p>To find the best topic sentence in STEP, read the supporting sentences first and ask: What do all of these sentences have in common? Then choose the option that names that common idea. Wrong options are usually (1) one of the details, (2) a general statement that is too big, or (3) a sentence about a related but different topic.</p>\n<p><strong>Examples:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>✓</strong> Cows are very useful animals. (topic: cows · controlling idea: useful)</p>\n<p><strong>details</strong> They give us milk and cheese. Their skin is used for shoes. They work in the fields.</p>\n<p><strong>✗ narrow</strong> Shoes are made of leather. (only one detail)</p>\n<p><strong>✗ broad</strong> Animals live everywhere in the world. (too general)</p>\n<p><strong>✗ off</strong> Farmers work very hard. (a related but different topic)</p>\n<p><strong>✓</strong> Our hotel in Dubai was excellent. (covers the pool, the restaurants and the rooms)</p>\n<p><strong>✓</strong> There are several easy ways to save money. (a good opening for a list of ideas)</p>\n<p><strong>✓</strong> Travel in Saudi Arabia has changed a lot over the years. (covers the past and the present)</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">المهارة</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">جملة الموضوع غالبًا هي أول جملة في الفقرة، ولها جزءان: الموضوع والفكرة المسيطرة (ما يريد الكاتب قوله عن الموضوع). والجملة الجيدة ليست ضيقة جدًا (تذكر تفصيلة واحدة) ولا واسعة جدًا (تصلح لمئة فقرة)، بل تشمل كل الجمل الداعمة بدقة. اقرأ الجمل الداعمة أولًا واسأل: ما الفكرة المشتركة بينها؟ ثم اختر البديل الذي يذكرها.</span></p>\n<h3>Strategy</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>1. Skip the blank and read all the supporting sentences first.</p>\n<p>2. Write the common idea in three or four words (useful animals, ways to travel).</p>\n<p>3. Choose the option that contains BOTH the topic and that idea.</p>\n<p>4. Reject options that are only one detail (too narrow) or that could fit any paragraph (too broad).</p>\n<p>5. Reject options about a related topic that the paragraph does not discuss.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">تجاوز الفراغ واقرأ الجمل الداعمة أولًا، واكتب الفكرة المشتركة في كلمات قليلة، واختر البديل الذي يحتوي على الموضوع والفكرة معًا، وارفض البديل الضيق والبديل الواسع والبديل المتعلق بموضوع آخر.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Traps and Common Mistakes</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>✗ A detail from the paragraph offered as the topic sentence (too narrow).</p>\n<p>✗ A very general statement (too broad).</p>\n<p>✗ A sentence on a related topic that shares a word with the paragraph.</p>\n<p>✗ A sentence about one example only, when the paragraph lists several examples.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Worked STEP Examples (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>Example 1. Which sentence is the best topic sentence for the paragraph?</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>______ It teaches you patience. It helps you relax after a busy day. You can also eat the fish you catch.</p>\n<p>A. Fishing is a relaxing and useful hobby.</p>\n<p>B. Fish live in the sea.</p>\n<p>C. I went fishing with my uncle last Friday.</p>\n<p>D. Hobbies are important for everyone.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Read the details: patience, relaxing, eating the fish.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Common idea: the benefits of fishing.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> 'Fish live in the sea' is off the topic, 'last Friday' is one event, and 'Hobbies are important' is too broad.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Answer: A</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الفكرة المشتركة فوائد صيد السمك، والبدائل الأخرى إما خارج الموضوع أو ضيقة أو واسعة.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 2. Which sentence would be the best topic sentence for a paragraph about the problems of fast food?</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. Burgers were first made in America.</p>\n<p>B. I ate pizza last night.</p>\n<p>C. Eating too much fast food can cause several problems.</p>\n<p>D. Fast food restaurants open late.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The paragraph must be about problems of fast food.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The topic sentence needs both ideas: fast food + problems.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Only 'Eating too much fast food can cause several problems' has both.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Answer: C</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">جملة الموضوع تحتاج الموضوع والفكرة المسيطرة معًا.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 3. Which sentence is the best topic sentence for the paragraph?</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>______ Some people play sports such as football and volleyball. Others prefer quiet activities like reading or drawing. Many families simply spend time together at the park.</p>\n<p>A. Football is the most popular sport.</p>\n<p>B. People spend their free time in different ways.</p>\n<p>C. Parks are green and clean.</p>\n<p>D. Free time is short during exams.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Details: sports, quiet activities, time at the park.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Common idea: different ways to spend free time.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The football and park options are only one detail each.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Answer: B</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الجملة الصحيحة تشمل كل الأنشطة المذكورة.</span></p>\n<h3>Writing Task W-A2-01 — A hobby I enjoy</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>Task:</strong> Write a paragraph of 60–90 words about a hobby you enjoy. Begin with a clear topic sentence that names the hobby and says what you feel or think about it.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">اكتب فقرة من ستين إلى تسعين كلمة عن هواية تستمتع بها، وابدأها بجملة موضوع واضحة تذكر الهواية ورأيك فيها.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Planning frame</strong></p>\n<p>1. Topic sentence: What is your hobby, and what do you think about it?</p>\n<p>2. When and how did you start?</p>\n<p>3. What do you do, and where?</p>\n<p>4. What does the hobby teach you or give you?</p>\n<p>5. An example or a special moment.</p>\n<p>6. Closing sentence: your hope or feeling for the future.</p>\n<p><strong>Model answer (75 words; target 60–90)</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>My favourite hobby is photography. I started taking photos two years ago when my father gave me an old camera. Now I take pictures of birds, buildings and the sunset. Every Friday, I go to the park near our house to practise. Photography teaches me to be patient and to notice small details. Last month, one of my photos won a prize in a school competition. I hope to become a professional photographer one day.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Examiner's commentary</strong></p>\n<p>▸ The topic sentence names the hobby clearly and introduces the whole paragraph.</p>\n<p>▸ Every supporting sentence is about photography: how it started, what, where and why.</p>\n<p>▸ A specific example (the prize) makes the paragraph interesting.</p>\n<p>▸ The closing sentence looks to the future and ends the paragraph naturally.</p>\n<p><strong>Self-check before you hand in</strong></p>\n<p>☐ Does my first sentence name the hobby and give my opinion?</p>\n<p>☐ Do all my sentences support the topic sentence?</p>\n<p>☐ Did I give at least one specific example?</p>\n<p>☐ Is my paragraph 60–90 words?</p>\n<p>☐ Did I check tenses, capital letters and full stops?</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">تأكد من أن جملتك الأولى تذكر الهواية ورأيك فيها، وأن كل الجمل تدعمها، وأنك أعطيت مثالًا محددًا.</span></p>","wu":"Worked examples: Example 1 A · Example 2 C · Example 3 B","quiz":[{"l":["Answer all 30 questions. Read each paragraph or sentence carefully and choose the best answer (A, B, C or D).","أجب عن الأسئلة الثلاثين جميعها. اقرأ كل فقرة أو جملة بعناية واختر الإجابة الصحيحة من بين البدائل الأربعة.","Part A — Lesson Focus (Questions 1–20)","الجزء الأول: أسئلة على مهارة الدرس."],"q":[{"n":1,"s":"Which sentence is the best topic sentence for the paragraph?","o":["My bike is blue and black.","Cycling is a great way to travel around the city.","Cars are faster than bikes.","The environment is important."],"x":["______ It is quick, cheap and good for the environment. It also keeps you fit. I ride mine to school every day."],"k":1,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis] Cycling is a great way to travel around the city. — The details are advantages of cycling.","h":"التفاصيل مزايا ركوب الدراجة."},{"n":2,"s":"Which sentence is the best topic sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Shoes are made of leather.","Farmers work very hard.","Cows are very useful animals.","Animals live everywhere in the world."],"x":["______ They give us milk, cheese and butter. Their skin is used to make shoes and bags. Farmers also use them to work in the fields."],"k":2,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis] Cows are very useful animals. — All the details show how cows are useful.","h":"التفاصيل تبين فائدة الأبقار."},{"n":3,"s":"Which sentence is the best topic sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Our hotel in Dubai was excellent.","Swimming is good exercise.","I love eating at restaurants.","Dubai is in the United Arab Emirates."],"x":["______ First, it has a big swimming pool. Second, there are many restaurants with different kinds of food. Finally, the rooms are clean and comfortable."],"k":0,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis] Our hotel in Dubai was excellent. — Pool, restaurants and rooms are reasons the hotel was excellent.","h":"الأسباب تصف الفندق."},{"n":4,"s":"Which sentence is the best topic sentence for the paragraph?","o":["The school bus is always late.","Students at our school travel to school in different ways.","Walking is healthy.","Our school has a big car park."],"x":["______ Some students walk, and others come by bus. Many students come with their parents by car. A few students ride bicycles."],"k":1,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis] Students at our school travel to school in different ways. — The details list different ways of travelling to school.","h":"التفاصيل طرق مختلفة للوصول إلى المدرسة."},{"n":5,"s":"Which sentence is the best topic sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Football is an easy game to play.","Footballs are round.","Sports are fun.","My friends live near the park."],"x":["______ You need only a ball and some friends. You can play it in the street, in a park or on the beach. That is why children everywhere love it."],"k":0,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis] Football is an easy game to play. — The details show why football is easy to play.","h":"التفاصيل تبين سهولة كرة القدم."},{"n":6,"s":"Which sentence is the best topic sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Honey is good for your health.","Mountains are very high.","I visited my grandmother last year.","Al-Baha is a wonderful place to visit."],"x":["______ The weather is cool all year. There are green mountains and beautiful valleys. Visitors can also buy honey and fresh fruit."],"k":3,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis] Al-Baha is a wonderful place to visit. — The details describe what makes a place good to visit.","h":"التفاصيل تصف مكانًا سياحيًا."},{"n":7,"s":"Which sentence is the best topic sentence for the paragraph?","o":["My mother does a lot for our family.","Lunch is at two o'clock.","My homework is difficult.","Mothers are important in every country."],"x":["______ For example, she cooks lunch for us every day. She also helps us with our homework. In the evening, she listens to our problems."],"k":0,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis] My mother does a lot for our family. — The examples show what the mother does for the family; the last option is too broad.","h":"الأمثلة عن عطاء الأم."},{"n":8,"s":"Which sentence is the best topic sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Shopping centres are busy at night.","Saudi Arabia is a big country.","My uncle works in Riyadh.","Riyadh is the largest city in Saudi Arabia."],"x":["______ It has many tall buildings and large shopping centres. Millions of people live and work there. It is also the capital of the country."],"k":3,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis] Riyadh is the largest city in Saudi Arabia. — The details describe one big city, Riyadh.","h":"التفاصيل عن مدينة الرياض."},{"n":9,"s":"Which sentence would be the best topic sentence for a paragraph about how to save money?","o":["Money is made of paper.","My brother bought a new phone yesterday.","There are several easy ways to save money.","Banks open at eight o'clock."],"k":2,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis] There are several easy ways to save money. — It introduces a list of ways to save money.","h":"تقدّم قائمة بطرق التوفير."},{"n":10,"s":"Which sentence is the best topic sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Ahmed is my best friend.","Newspapers are cheap.","Many people in my life enjoy reading.","Buses are crowded in the morning."],"x":["______ Ahmed reads every night before bed. Sara reads on the bus. Our teacher reads the newspaper during the break."],"k":2,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis] Many people in my life enjoy reading. — Three different people who read: the common idea is reading.","h":"ثلاثة أشخاص يقرؤون."},{"n":11,"s":"Which sentence is the best topic sentence for the paragraph?","o":["The ostrich is an unusual bird.","Many birds can fly.","Eggs are good for breakfast.","Some animals have long necks."],"x":["______ It has a long neck, long legs and a small head. It can run very fast, but it cannot fly. It lays very big eggs."],"k":0,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis] The ostrich is an unusual bird. — All the details describe the ostrich.","h":"التفاصيل تصف النعامة."},{"n":12,"s":"Which sentence is the best topic sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Photos are nice to keep.","Shops are open until midnight.","My phone is three years old.","Mobile phones are useful in many ways."],"x":["______ We use them to call our families and send messages. We also use them to take photos and find our way. Some people even use them to pay in shops."],"k":3,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis] Mobile phones are useful in many ways. — The details are different uses of mobile phones.","h":"التفاصيل استخدامات الهاتف."},{"n":13,"s":"Which sentence would be the best topic sentence for a paragraph about the benefits of drinking water?","o":["Drinking enough water is good for your body in many ways.","Water is H2O.","I drink juice at breakfast.","Some people buy bottled water."],"k":0,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis] Drinking enough water is good for your body in many ways. — It names the topic (drinking water) and the idea (benefits).","h":"تذكر الموضوع والفوائد."},{"n":14,"s":"Which sentence is the best topic sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Flowers need water and sun.","The market is open in the evening.","Farmers in our village work hard all day.","Vegetables are healthy."],"x":["______ In the morning, they water the flowers and cut the grass. In the afternoon, they pick vegetables. In the evening, they sell them at the market."],"k":2,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis] Farmers in our village work hard all day. — The details describe the farmers' working day.","h":"التفاصيل يوم عمل المزارعين."},{"n":15,"s":"Which sentence is the best topic sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Travelling is expensive.","I study English at school.","Many people want good jobs.","Learning a second language has many advantages."],"x":["______ It helps you understand people from other countries. It can help you get a good job. It also makes travelling easier."],"k":3,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis] Learning a second language has many advantages. — The details are advantages of learning a language.","h":"التفاصيل مزايا تعلم لغة ثانية."},{"n":16,"s":"Which sentence is the best topic sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Winter is cold in the north.","Penguins live in Antarctica.","Nests are made of sticks.","Birds live in many different ways."],"x":["______ Some fly south in winter. Others build nests in the same place every year. A few, like penguins, cannot fly at all."],"k":3,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis] Birds live in many different ways. — The details show different ways that birds live.","h":"التفاصيل طرق مختلفة لحياة الطيور."},{"n":17,"s":"Which sentence is the best topic sentence for the paragraph?","o":["There are some simple rules for staying clean and healthy.","Soap is cheap.","Teeth are white.","I have a shower in the morning."],"x":["______ Wash your hands before you eat. Brush your teeth twice a day. Have a shower every day."],"k":0,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis] There are some simple rules for staying clean and healthy. — The details are rules for staying clean.","h":"التفاصيل قواعد للنظافة."},{"n":18,"s":"Which sentence is the best topic sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Camels are strong animals.","Travel in Saudi Arabia has changed a lot over the years.","Flying is the safest way to travel.","Jeddah is on the Red Sea."],"x":["______ In the past, people travelled across the desert on camels, and journeys took weeks. Later, cars and roads made travel faster. Today, people can fly from Riyadh to Jeddah in less than two hours."],"k":1,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis] Travel in Saudi Arabia has changed a lot over the years. — The details move from the past to today: travel has changed.","h":"التفاصيل تنتقل من الماضي إلى الحاضر."},{"n":19,"s":"Which sentence is the best topic sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Video calls are free.","Doctors work long hours.","Students like online games.","The internet helps many different people."],"x":["______ Older people can talk to their grandchildren by video. Students can take online classes. Doctors can see patients who live far away."],"k":3,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis] The internet helps many different people. — Three groups of people helped by the internet.","h":"ثلاث فئات يساعدها الإنترنت."},{"n":20,"s":"Which sentence is the best topic sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Students should go to bed at nine.","The brain is very complex.","Sleep is very important for students.","Many students feel tired in class."],"x":["______ During sleep, the brain stores what we learned during the day. Sleep also gives the body energy for the next day. Without enough sleep, students feel tired and cannot concentrate."],"k":2,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis] Sleep is very important for students. — The details explain why sleep matters for students.","h":"التفاصيل تشرح أهمية النوم للطلاب."}]},{"l":["Part B — Mixed STEP Composition Analysis (Questions 21–30)","الجزء الثاني: أسئلة متنوعة من قسم تحليل الكتابة في اختبار STEP."],"q":[{"n":21,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 3","Sentence 4","Sentence 5","Sentence 6"],"x":["(1) My hobby is collecting stamps. (2) I have more than three hundred stamps. (3) Some of them are from Japan and Brazil. (4) My brother collects football shirts. (5) I keep them in a special book. (6) My grandfather gave me my first stamp."],"k":1,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 4 — The paragraph is about the writer's stamps; the brother's football shirts are off the topic.","h":"قمصان الأخ خارج موضوع الطوابع."},{"n":22,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["3 – 4 – 1 – 2","1 – 3 – 4 – 2","3 – 1 – 4 – 2","3 – 1 – 2 – 4"],"x":["(1) Next, I make small holes in the bottom.","(2) Finally, I put the seeds in and water them.","(3) First, I cut an old plastic bottle in half.","(4) After that, I fill the bottle with soil."],"k":2,"e":"[best order] 3 – 1 – 4 – 2 — First → Next → After that → Finally.","h":"رتّب حسب كلمات التسلسل."},{"n":23,"s":"Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?","o":["The club is near the airport.","I hope to become a great swimmer one day.","My coach is from Egypt.","Football is popular too."],"x":["Swimming is my favourite sport. I swim three times a week at the club. It makes my body strong and helps me sleep well. My coach says I can join the team next year. ______"],"k":1,"e":"[concluding sentence] I hope to become a great swimmer one day. — The closing sentence returns to swimming with a hope.","h":"الخاتمة تعود إلى السباحة مع أمل."},{"n":24,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["so","or","because","but"],"x":["The film was long, ______ it was very interesting."],"k":3,"e":"[transition / connector] but — long / interesting is a contrast.","h":"التضاد يحتاج but."},{"n":25,"s":"My (A) brother and I (B) enjoys (C) playing chess (D) in the evening.","o":["brother","enjoys","playing","in the evening"],"k":1,"e":"[error] enjoys — My brother and I is plural: enjoy.","h":"الفاعل جمع فالفعل enjoy."},{"n":26,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["Drawing paper is expensive.","My teacher is very tall.","At first, my drawings were very simple.","Animals are hard to find."],"x":["I started learning to draw last year. ______ Now I can draw people and animals. My teacher says my drawings are much better."],"k":2,"e":"[complete the paragraph] At first, my drawings were very simple. — 'Now I can draw' needs a contrast with the beginning.","h":"Now تحتاج مقارنة بالبداية."},{"n":27,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 1","Sentence 2","Sentence 3","Sentence 4"],"x":["(1) Our school canteen sells healthy food. (2) My favourite TV programme is about cars. (3) You can buy fruit, salads and sandwiches. (4) Fizzy drinks are not allowed. (5) The prices are low for students."],"k":1,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 2 — The TV programme is off the topic of the canteen.","h":"البرنامج التلفزيوني خارج موضوع المقصف."},{"n":28,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["so","but","or","because"],"x":["I forgot my umbrella, ______ I got wet."],"k":0,"e":"[transition / connector] so — Getting wet is the result.","h":"النتيجة تحتاج so."},{"n":29,"s":"(A) Last year, my (B) family (C) travels to Malaysia (D) by plane.","o":["Last","family","travels","by"],"k":2,"e":"[error] travels — Last year needs the past tense: travelled.","h":"الماضي travelled."},{"n":30,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["4 – 2 – 3 – 1","2 – 4 – 1 – 3","4 – 1 – 2 – 3","4 – 2 – 1 – 3"],"x":["(1) English","(2) has studied","(3) for three years","(4) My cousin"],"k":3,"e":"[best order] 4 – 2 – 1 – 3 — My cousin has studied English for three years.","h":"فاعل ثم فعل ثم مفعول ثم مدة."}]}],"n":30},{"id":"2.2","t":"Supporting Sentences and Examples","html":"<p><strong>Unit 2 · Lesson 2.2 · CEFR A2 · STEP link: Composition Analysis (10%)</strong></p>\n<h3>Objectives</h3>\n<p>1. Support a topic sentence with reasons and examples.</p>\n<p>2. Choose the best supporting sentence for a gap.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الأهداف</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">١. أن يدعم الطالب جملة الموضوع بالأسباب والأمثلة.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٢. أن يختار أفضل جملة داعمة لملء فراغ في فقرة.</span></p>\n<h3>The Skill</h3>\n<p>Supporting sentences come after the topic sentence and PROVE or EXPLAIN it. They give reasons (because …), examples (for example, …), facts and numbers (It has 3,000 books) or short stories from experience. A paragraph with a topic sentence but no strong support is weak and unconvincing.</p>\n<p>Good support is SPECIFIC. Compare: 'The library is good' (general, weak) and 'The library has 3,000 books and six computers for research' (specific, strong). Useful phrases for support are: For example, … / For instance, … / Such as … / First, … Second, … / Another reason is … / Also, …</p>\n<p>In STEP, complete-the-paragraph items remove one supporting sentence. The correct sentence must (1) stay on the topic, (2) connect to the sentences before AND after the gap, and (3) fit the signal words around it. If the next sentence starts with also or another, the gap needs a first example of the same kind; if the gap comes after For example, it needs a specific example.</p>\n<p><strong>Examples:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>topic</strong> Exercise is good for your mind as well as your body.</p>\n<p><strong>reason</strong> It reduces stress after a long day at school.</p>\n<p><strong>example</strong> For example, a short run can make you feel happier.</p>\n<p><strong>fact</strong> Doctors say that thirty minutes of walking a day is enough.</p>\n<p><strong>✗ weak</strong> Exercise is nice. (too general to support anything)</p>\n<p><strong>✗ off</strong> My father likes football. (about one person, not about the mind and body)</p>\n<p><strong>signal</strong> Students can borrow books. ______ Children can also join reading clubs. (the gap needs another group of people)</p>\n<p><strong>signal</strong> He gives me good advice. For example, ______ (the gap needs a specific piece of advice)</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">المهارة</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الجمل الداعمة تأتي بعد جملة الموضوع لتثبتها أو تشرحها بالأسباب والأمثلة والحقائق والأرقام والقصص القصيرة، والدعم الجيد محدد لا عام. وفي أسئلة إكمال الفقرة يجب أن تبقى الجملة الصحيحة في الموضوع، وأن ترتبط بما قبل الفراغ وما بعده، وأن تناسب كلمات الإشارة مثل also وanother وFor example.</span></p>\n<h3>Strategy</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>1. Read the topic sentence and write its controlling idea.</p>\n<p>2. Read the sentence before AND after the gap.</p>\n<p>3. Look for signal words: also, another, for example, then, as a result.</p>\n<p>4. Choose the option that is specific and supports the controlling idea.</p>\n<p>5. Read the whole paragraph with your answer to check that it flows.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">اقرأ جملة الموضوع وحدد فكرتها المسيطرة، واقرأ الجملة قبل الفراغ وبعده، وابحث عن كلمات الإشارة، واختر البديل المحدد الذي يدعم الفكرة، ثم اقرأ الفقرة كاملة بإجابتك.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Traps and Common Mistakes</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>✗ A sentence that is on the general subject but does not support the controlling idea.</p>\n<p>✗ A sentence that ignores a signal word after the gap (also, another).</p>\n<p>✗ A general sentence where the paragraph needs a specific example.</p>\n<p>✗ A detail about a person or place that is mentioned but is not the topic.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Worked STEP Examples (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>Example 1. Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Our school has many activities after classes. There is a football club and a science club. ______ Students can choose what they like.</p>\n<p>A. Classes finish at one o'clock.</p>\n<p>B. Football is played with eleven players.</p>\n<p>C. There is also a drawing club for artists.</p>\n<p>D. Science is a difficult subject.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Controlling idea: many activities after classes.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The sentence before lists two clubs; the gap should add another activity.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> 'There is also a drawing club for artists' continues the list.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Answer: C</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الجملة الصحيحة تضيف نشاطًا آخر إلى القائمة.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 2. Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>(1)</strong> Honey is a natural and healthy food. <strong>(2)</strong> Bees make it from flowers. <strong>(3)</strong> It can help when you have a sore throat. <strong>(4)</strong> Sugar is used in many cakes. <strong>(5)</strong> People eat it with bread or add it to tea. <strong>(6)</strong> Some of the best honey comes from Saudi mountains.</p>\n<p>A. Sentence 3 B. Sentence 4 C. Sentence 5 D. Sentence 6</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Topic: honey is natural and healthy.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Check each sentence: bees, sore throat, eating it, Saudi honey all support it.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Sentence 4 about sugar is a different topic, even though it is also sweet.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Answer: B</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الجملة الرابعة عن السكر لا عن العسل.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 3. Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Learning to swim is important. It is good exercise for the whole body. ______ Every child should learn to swim.</p>\n<p>A. Swimming pools are often crowded.</p>\n<p>B. Some people swim in the sea.</p>\n<p>C. Swimming costumes are colourful.</p>\n<p>D. More importantly, it can save your life in the water.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Controlling idea: learning to swim is important.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The paragraph gives reasons; the gap needs a second, stronger reason.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Only 'it can save your life' is a reason for its importance.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Answer: D</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">اختر السبب الذي يدعم أهمية تعلم السباحة.</span></p>\n<h3>Writing Task W-A2-02 — Why I like our school library</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>Task:</strong> Write 60–90 words explaining why you like your school library (or another place at school). Give at least two reasons and one specific example.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">اكتب من ستين إلى تسعين كلمة تشرح فيها لماذا تحب مكتبة مدرستك (أو مكانًا آخر في المدرسة)، وقدّم سببين على الأقل ومثالًا محددًا.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Planning frame</strong></p>\n<p>1. Topic sentence: I like … for … reasons.</p>\n<p>2. First reason + detail.</p>\n<p>3. Second reason + a specific example (For example, …).</p>\n<p>4. Third reason or extra fact (a number, a name).</p>\n<p>5. Closing sentence: For all these reasons, …</p>\n<p><strong>Model answer (75 words; target 60–90)</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I like our school library for three reasons. First, it is quiet, so I can concentrate on my homework. Second, it has many interesting books. For example, I recently read a book about the history of Makkah and another about space. Third, the librarian, Mr. Hassan, always helps us find the right information for our projects. The library also has six computers for research. For all these reasons, it is my favourite place at school.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Examiner's commentary</strong></p>\n<p>▸ The topic sentence tells the reader to expect three reasons.</p>\n<p>▸ First, Second and Third organize the support clearly.</p>\n<p>▸ The example (books about Makkah and space) and the fact (six computers) make the support specific.</p>\n<p>▸ The closing sentence repeats the main idea in new words.</p>\n<p><strong>Self-check before you hand in</strong></p>\n<p>☐ Does my topic sentence say what I like and why?</p>\n<p>☐ Did I give at least two clear reasons?</p>\n<p>☐ Did I use For example to give a specific example?</p>\n<p>☐ Is every sentence about my topic?</p>\n<p>☐ Is my paragraph 60–90 words?</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">تأكد من وجود سببين على الأقل ومثال محدد، ومن أن كل جملة تدعم جملة الموضوع.</span></p>","wu":"Worked examples: Example 1 C · Example 2 B · Example 3 D","quiz":[{"l":["Answer all 30 questions. Read each paragraph or sentence carefully and choose the best answer (A, B, C or D).","أجب عن الأسئلة الثلاثين جميعها. اقرأ كل فقرة أو جملة بعناية واختر الإجابة الصحيحة من بين البدائل الأربعة.","Part A — Lesson Focus (Questions 1–20)","الجزء الأول: أسئلة على مهارة الدرس."],"q":[{"n":1,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["Next to it, there is a pharmacy and a bakery.","My aunt lives in Dammam.","I don't like going shopping.","Parks are found in every city."],"x":["Our neighbourhood has many useful places. There is a big supermarket at the end of our street. ______ There is also a park where children can play."],"k":0,"e":"[complete the paragraph] Next to it, there is a pharmacy and a bakery. — The gap needs more useful places in the neighbourhood.","h":"الفراغ يحتاج أماكن مفيدة أخرى."},{"n":2,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["Many people go to the gym.","My father likes football.","Gyms are expensive.","For example, a short run can make you feel happier."],"x":["Exercise is good for your mind as well as your body. ______ It also helps you sleep better at night."],"k":3,"e":"[complete the paragraph] For example, a short run can make you feel happier. — The gap needs an example of exercise helping the mind.","h":"مثال على فائدة الرياضة للعقل."},{"n":3,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["Homes can be big or small.","My mother likes cooking.","You can make your bed every morning.","Dinner is at eight o'clock."],"x":["There are many ways to help at home. ______ You can also wash the dishes after dinner. Even small jobs help your family."],"k":2,"e":"[complete the paragraph] You can make your bed every morning. — 'You can also' needs a first way of helping before it.","h":"also تحتاج طريقة أولى قبلها."},{"n":4,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["He is seventy-two years old.","For example, he told me to study a little every day.","He lives in a village.","Exams are difficult."],"x":["My grandfather is very wise. He always gives me good advice. ______ That advice helped me a lot during my exams."],"k":1,"e":"[complete the paragraph] For example, he told me to study a little every day. — 'That advice' needs a specific piece of advice before it.","h":"That advice تحتاج نصيحة محددة قبلها."},{"n":5,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["Turtles can live for many years.","Jellyfish are beautiful.","The sea is blue.","Birds can also get caught in plastic rings."],"x":["Plastic is dangerous for sea animals. Turtles sometimes eat plastic bags because they look like jellyfish. ______ We must keep plastic out of the sea."],"k":3,"e":"[complete the paragraph] Birds can also get caught in plastic rings. — The gap needs another example of the danger of plastic.","h":"مثال آخر على خطر البلاستيك."},{"n":6,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["For example, they can visit the old houses in Al-Balad.","Jeddah is very humid in summer.","Many people live in Jeddah.","Tourists take a lot of photos."],"x":["Jeddah has many places for tourists. ______ Tourists can also walk along the Corniche and enjoy the sea."],"k":0,"e":"[complete the paragraph] For example, they can visit the old houses in Al-Balad. — 'Tourists can also' needs a first place before it.","h":"also تحتاج مكانًا أول قبلها."},{"n":7,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["Libraries were built long ago.","My brother is a student.","Books are expensive in shops.","Adults can read newspapers and use the computers."],"x":["Public libraries are useful for everyone. Students can borrow books for their projects. ______ Children can join reading clubs on Saturdays."],"k":3,"e":"[complete the paragraph] Adults can read newspapers and use the computers. — The paragraph lists groups of people who use libraries.","h":"الفقرة تذكر فئات تستفيد من المكتبة."},{"n":8,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["Some words are long.","People speak many languages.","Say 'thank you' when someone helps you.","Happy people smile a lot."],"x":["Being polite is important. Say 'please' when you ask for something. ______ These small words make people happy."],"k":2,"e":"[complete the paragraph] Say 'thank you' when someone helps you. — 'These small words' needs another polite word before it.","h":"These small words تحتاج كلمة مهذبة أخرى."},{"n":9,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["Science is taught in English.","Her brother likes art.","She always gets the highest marks in her class.","The science fair was in March."],"x":["My cousin is very good at science. ______ She also won first prize in the school science fair."],"k":2,"e":"[complete the paragraph] She always gets the highest marks in her class. — The gap needs proof that she is good at science.","h":"الفراغ يحتاج دليلًا على تفوقها."},{"n":10,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["Smartphones have good cameras.","Phones are cheaper now.","Some students like science.","Others spend hours on games instead of studying."],"x":["Smartphones can cause some problems. Some students use them late at night and do not sleep enough. ______ As a result, their marks may go down."],"k":3,"e":"[complete the paragraph] Others spend hours on games instead of studying. — 'Some students … Others …' — the gap needs a second problem.","h":"Some … Others تحتاج مشكلة ثانية."},{"n":11,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["Dates grow on palm trees.","They have a lot of fibre, which helps digestion.","Many people sell dates.","Chocolate is sweet too."],"x":["Dates are a healthy snack. They are full of energy. ______ They also contain vitamins and minerals."],"k":1,"e":"[complete the paragraph] They have a lot of fibre, which helps digestion. — The gap needs another health benefit of dates.","h":"فائدة صحية أخرى للتمر."},{"n":12,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["The bus left at eight.","Dinosaurs lived long ago.","My friend was sick that day.","Then we did experiments with electricity."],"x":["Our class trip to the science museum was exciting. We saw a real dinosaur skeleton. ______ At the end, we watched a film about space."],"k":3,"e":"[complete the paragraph] Then we did experiments with electricity. — The gap needs another exciting event in the middle of the trip.","h":"حدث مثير آخر في وسط الرحلة."},{"n":13,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["Summer is hot in Riyadh.","Tabuk is a big city.","At night, the temperature can fall below zero.","People like warm drinks."],"x":["Winter in the north of Saudi Arabia can be very cold. ______ Sometimes, it even snows in Tabuk."],"k":2,"e":"[complete the paragraph] At night, the temperature can fall below zero. — The gap needs a detail that shows how cold it is.","h":"تفصيلة تبين شدة البرد."},{"n":14,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 3","Sentence 4","Sentence 5","Sentence 6"],"x":["(1) Our school library is a great place to study. (2) It is quiet and has comfortable chairs. (3) There are thousands of books on many subjects. (4) The librarian helps students find information. (5) The school canteen sells sandwiches and juice. (6) I go there every day during the break."],"k":2,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 5 — The canteen does not support the idea that the library is good for studying.","h":"المقصف لا يدعم فكرة المكتبة."},{"n":15,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 2","Sentence 3","Sentence 4","Sentence 5"],"x":["(1) Recycling helps protect the environment. (2) It reduces the amount of rubbish. (3) My uncle's new car is electric. (4) It saves trees because we reuse paper. (5) It also saves energy. (6) Everyone should recycle at home."],"k":1,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 3 — The electric car is about the environment, but it is not about recycling.","h":"السيارة الكهربائية ليست عن إعادة التدوير."},{"n":16,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 2","Sentence 3","Sentence 4","Sentence 5"],"x":["(1) My father has an interesting job. (2) He is an air traffic controller. (3) He helps planes take off and land safely. (4) Planes are very expensive to buy. (5) He has to stay calm all the time."],"k":2,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 4 — The price of planes does not describe the father's job.","h":"سعر الطائرات لا يصف عمل الأب."},{"n":17,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 1","Sentence 2","Sentence 3","Sentence 4"],"x":["(1) Breakfast is the most important meal of the day. (2) Lunch at our school is at twelve o'clock. (3) It gives you energy for the morning. (4) It helps you concentrate in class. (5) A good breakfast includes eggs, bread and fruit. (6) Don't leave home without breakfast."],"k":1,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 2 — The lunch time does not support the importance of breakfast.","h":"موعد الغداء خارج موضوع الإفطار."},{"n":18,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 4","Sentence 5","Sentence 6","Sentence 7"],"x":["(1) Our town has a new sports centre. (2) It has a swimming pool and a gym. (3) There are also courts for basketball and tennis. (4) My cousin is studying in London. (5) Coaches give lessons for children. (6) It is open every day until eleven. (7) Many families use it at weekends."],"k":0,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 4 — The cousin in London is off the topic of the sports centre.","h":"ابن العم في لندن خارج الموضوع."},{"n":19,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 3","Sentence 4","Sentence 5","Sentence 6"],"x":["(1) The camel is well suited to desert life. (2) It can drink a lot of water at once. (3) Its hump stores fat for energy. (4) Its long eyelashes protect its eyes from sand. (5) Its wide feet do not sink into the sand. (6) Horses need a lot of water every day."],"k":3,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 6 — Horses do not support the idea that camels suit the desert.","h":"الخيول لا تدعم فكرة تكيّف الجمل."},{"n":20,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["Many volunteers are adults.","Teams usually have a leader.","It also helps them learn new skills, such as planning and communication.","Communities are different in each city."],"x":["Volunteering is good for young people. It teaches them to work in a team. ______ Finally, it makes them feel useful in their community."],"k":2,"e":"[complete the paragraph] It also helps them learn new skills, such as planning and communication. — The gap needs a second benefit between the first and the last (Finally).","h":"الفراغ يحتاج فائدة ثانية قبل Finally."}]},{"l":["Part B — Mixed STEP Composition Analysis (Questions 21–30)","الجزء الثاني: أسئلة متنوعة من قسم تحليل الكتابة في اختبار STEP."],"q":[{"n":21,"s":"Which sentence is the best topic sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Fried rice is a quick and simple meal.","Rice grows in water.","Vegetables are healthy.","My mother cooks every day."],"x":["______ It is cheap and easy to make. You can eat it hot or cold. You can also add many vegetables."],"k":0,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis] Fried rice is a quick and simple meal. — The details describe an easy, flexible meal.","h":"التفاصيل تصف وجبة سهلة."},{"n":22,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["because","so","but","or"],"x":["My friend lives far away, ______ we talk on the phone every week."],"k":2,"e":"[transition / connector] but — far away / talk every week is a contrast.","h":"التضاد يحتاج but."},{"n":23,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["2 – 3 – 1 – 4","2 – 1 – 3 – 4","3 – 2 – 1 – 4","2 – 3 – 4 – 1"],"x":["(1) Then she paid at the cashier.","(2) Reem took a basket at the door.","(3) She put milk, bread and eggs in it.","(4) Finally, she carried the bags home."],"k":0,"e":"[best order] 2 – 3 – 1 – 4 — took a basket → filled it → paid → carried home.","h":"رتّب خطوات التسوق."},{"n":24,"s":"There (A) is many (B) books on (C) the shelves (D) in my room.","o":["is","books","the","in"],"k":0,"e":"[error] is — many books is plural: There are.","h":"الجمع يحتاج there are."},{"n":25,"s":"Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Songs are easy to remember.","Thanks to her, we all enjoy learning English.","Ms. Mona has two children.","Stories can be long."],"x":["Our teacher, Ms. Mona, makes English lessons fun. She uses games and songs. She lets us act out stories. She always encourages us to speak. ______"],"k":1,"e":"[concluding sentence] Thanks to her, we all enjoy learning English. — The closing sentence sums up the effect of her teaching.","h":"الخاتمة تلخص أثر المعلمة."},{"n":26,"s":"Which sentence is correct?","o":["My brother don't like vegetables.","My brother not like vegetables.","My brother doesn't likes vegetables.","My brother doesn't like vegetables."],"k":3,"e":"[error] My brother doesn't like vegetables. — He / she + doesn't + base verb.","h":"doesn't ثم الفعل المجرد."},{"n":27,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["or","but","so","because"],"x":["We can go to the beach ______ we can visit the museum."],"k":0,"e":"[transition / connector] or — Two choices are joined with or.","h":"خياران يحتاجان or."},{"n":28,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 2","Sentence 3","Sentence 4","Sentence 5"],"x":["(1) Spring is my favourite season. (2) The weather is warm but not too hot. (3) My little sister started school this year. (4) Flowers grow in the desert after the rain. (5) We often have picnics outside."],"k":1,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 3 — The sister starting school is off the topic of spring.","h":"الجملة الثالثة خارج موضوع الربيع."},{"n":29,"s":"She (A) have (B) lived (C) in Taif (D) since 2020.","o":["have","lived","in","since"],"k":0,"e":"[error] have — She needs has: She has lived.","h":"She تحتاج has."},{"n":30,"s":"Which sentence would be the best topic sentence for a paragraph about the advantages of living near the sea?","o":["The sea is full of fish.","Life by the sea is healthy and enjoyable.","My uncle has a boat.","Some people live in the mountains."],"k":1,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis] Life by the sea is healthy and enjoyable. — It names the topic and a positive controlling idea.","h":"تذكر الموضوع وفكرة إيجابية."}]}],"n":30},{"id":"2.3","t":"Sequencing Words and Putting Sentences in Order","html":"<p><strong>Unit 2 · Lesson 2.3 · CEFR A2 · STEP link: Composition Analysis (10%)</strong></p>\n<h3>Objectives</h3>\n<p>1. Use sequencing words (first, next, then, finally).</p>\n<p>2. Put scrambled sentences in the best order.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الأهداف</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">١. أن يستخدم الطالب كلمات التسلسل (first وnext وthen وfinally).</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٢. أن يرتب الجمل المبعثرة في أفضل ترتيب.</span></p>\n<h3>The Skill</h3>\n<p>Many paragraphs follow TIME ORDER: a story (what happened first, next and last) or a process (how to make or do something). Sequencing words guide the reader: First, … / To begin with, … (start); Next, … / Then … / After that, … / Later, … (middle); Finally, … / In the end, … / At last, … (end).</p>\n<p>Some words show order inside a sentence: before, after, when, as soon as. 'Brush your teeth before you go to bed.' 'After school, I play football.' Time expressions also help: Last Friday … The next morning … A few minutes later …</p>\n<p>In STEP best-order items, you see four or five numbered sentences and choose the best order. Start by finding the FIRST sentence: it usually introduces the topic or the time (Last Friday, Badr went camping) and does not contain words like then, it, they or after that. Then follow the sequencing words and the pronouns: a sentence with they or it must come after the sentence that names the people or the thing.</p>\n<p><strong>Examples:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>start</strong> First, boil some water. · Last Friday, Badr went camping.</p>\n<p><strong>middle</strong> Next, … / Then … / After that, … / The next morning, …</p>\n<p><strong>end</strong> Finally, … / In the end, … / At last, …</p>\n<p><strong>before</strong> Turn off the lights before you leave the room.</p>\n<p><strong>after</strong> After I finished school, I went to my grandmother's house.</p>\n<p><strong>pronoun</strong> Majed lost his ball. (1st) → He looked everywhere for it. (2nd)</p>\n<p><strong>✗ → ✓</strong> Finally, read the question. First, write your answer. → First, read the question. Finally, write your answer.</p>\n<p><strong>✗ → ✓</strong> Then mix the flour and sugar. First, add the eggs. → First, mix the flour and sugar. Then add the eggs.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">المهارة</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">تتبع فقرات كثيرة الترتيب الزمني في القصص أو خطوات العمل، وترشد كلمات التسلسل القارئ: First للبداية، وNext وThen وAfter that للوسط، وFinally وIn the end للنهاية، إضافة إلى before وafter وwhen داخل الجملة. وفي أسئلة أفضل ترتيب ابحث أولًا عن الجملة الأولى التي تقدّم الموضوع أو الزمن ولا تحتوي على then أو they أو after that، ثم اتبع كلمات التسلسل والضمائر.</span></p>\n<h3>Strategy</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>1. Find the first sentence: it introduces the topic or the time and has no then, after that, it or they.</p>\n<p>2. Find the last sentence: Finally, In the end, At last, or a result.</p>\n<p>3. Use pronouns: a sentence with he, she, it or they comes after the sentence that names the person or thing.</p>\n<p>4. Check each option quickly: reject any option that does not start with your first sentence.</p>\n<p>5. Read your chosen order once from beginning to end to check that it makes sense.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">ابحث عن الجملة الأولى التي تقدم الموضوع أو الزمن، ثم الجملة الأخيرة التي فيها Finally أو In the end، واستخدم الضمائر لمعرفة الترتيب، واستبعد البدائل التي لا تبدأ بجملتك الأولى، ثم اقرأ الترتيب كاملًا للتأكد.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Traps and Common Mistakes</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>✗ An order that starts with a sentence containing Then or After that.</p>\n<p>✗ A pronoun (they, it) that comes before the noun it refers to.</p>\n<p>✗ Two sentences swapped in the middle when the logic needs a fixed order.</p>\n<p>✗ A sequencing word that does not match the position (Finally at the beginning).</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Worked STEP Examples (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>Example 1. Choose the best order for the sentences.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>(1)</strong> Then she put on her school uniform.</p>\n<p><strong>(2)</strong> Huda woke up at six.</p>\n<p><strong>(3)</strong> After that, she had breakfast.</p>\n<p><strong>(4)</strong> She washed her face first.</p>\n<p>A. 2 – 1 – 4 – 3 B. 2 – 4 – 1 – 3 C. 4 – 2 – 1 – 3 D. 2 – 4 – 3 – 1</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The first sentence introduces Huda and the time: sentence 2.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> 'She washed her face first' comes next; then 'Then … uniform'; then 'After that, … breakfast'.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The order is 2 – 4 – 1 – 3.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Answer: B</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">ابدأ بالجملة التي تذكر الاسم والزمن، ثم اتبع كلمات التسلسل.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 2. Which word or phrase best fills the blank?</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>______ you go to bed, brush your teeth.</p>\n<p>A. After B. Then C. Finally D. Before</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Which action is first? Brushing your teeth.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Going to bed comes later.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Before shows that the brushing comes first.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Answer: D</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">Before تعني أن الفعل الثاني يحدث أولًا.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 3. Choose the best order for the sentences.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>(1)</strong> At last, he found it under his bed.</p>\n<p><strong>(2)</strong> Majed couldn't find his football.</p>\n<p><strong>(3)</strong> Then he searched the garden.</p>\n<p><strong>(4)</strong> First, he looked in his room.</p>\n<p><strong>(5)</strong> But it wasn't there either.</p>\n<p>A. 2 – 4 – 3 – 5 – 1 B. 2 – 3 – 4 – 5 – 1</p>\n<p>C. 4 – 2 – 3 – 5 – 1 D. 2 – 4 – 5 – 3 – 1</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Sentence 2 names Majed and the problem, so it is first.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> First → Then → 'not there either' → At last.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The order is 2 – 4 – 3 – 5 – 1.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Answer: A</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الجملة التي تذكر الاسم والمشكلة أولًا، وAt last في النهاية.</span></p>\n<h3>Writing Task W-A2-03 — How to make a simple fruit salad</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>Task:</strong> Write 60–90 words explaining how to make a simple fruit salad. Use at least four sequencing words.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">اكتب من ستين إلى تسعين كلمة تشرح فيها طريقة عمل سلطة فواكه بسيطة، واستخدم أربع كلمات تسلسل على الأقل.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Planning frame</strong></p>\n<p>1. Topic sentence: Making a fruit salad is …</p>\n<p>2. First, … (wash the fruit)</p>\n<p>3. Next, … / Then … (peel and cut)</p>\n<p>4. After that, … (add honey or juice)</p>\n<p>5. Finally, … (chill and serve)</p>\n<p>6. Closing sentence: Your fruit salad is ready!</p>\n<p><strong>Model answer (78 words; target 60–90)</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Making a fruit salad is quick and easy. First, wash two apples, a banana, some grapes and an orange. Next, peel the banana and the orange. Then cut all the fruit into small pieces and put them in a large bowl. After that, add two spoons of honey and a little lemon juice. Mix everything gently with a big spoon. Finally, put the bowl in the fridge for twenty minutes. Your healthy fruit salad is ready to eat!</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Examiner's commentary</strong></p>\n<p>▸ The topic sentence introduces the process.</p>\n<p>▸ First, Next, Then, After that and Finally put the steps in a clear order.</p>\n<p>▸ Each step uses an imperative verb (wash, peel, cut, add, mix, put).</p>\n<p>▸ The closing sentence tells the reader that the process is complete.</p>\n<p><strong>Self-check before you hand in</strong></p>\n<p>☐ Did I use at least four sequencing words?</p>\n<p>☐ Are my steps in the correct order?</p>\n<p>☐ Did I use instruction verbs (wash, cut, add)?</p>\n<p>☐ Did I put a comma after First, Next, After that and Finally?</p>\n<p>☐ Is my paragraph 60–90 words?</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">تأكد من ترتيب الخطوات واستخدام كلمات التسلسل ووضع فاصلة بعدها، ومن استخدام أفعال الأمر.</span></p>","wu":"Worked examples: Example 1 B · Example 2 D · Example 3 A","quiz":[{"l":["Answer all 30 questions. Read each paragraph or sentence carefully and choose the best answer (A, B, C or D).","أجب عن الأسئلة الثلاثين جميعها. اقرأ كل فقرة أو جملة بعناية واختر الإجابة الصحيحة من بين البدائل الأربعة.","Part A — Lesson Focus (Questions 1–20)","الجزء الأول: أسئلة على مهارة الدرس."],"q":[{"n":1,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["2 – 1 – 4 – 3","2 – 4 – 1 – 3","4 – 2 – 1 – 3","2 – 4 – 3 – 1"],"x":["(1) Next, pour the hot water into the cup.","(2) First, boil some water in a kettle.","(3) Finally, take out the tea bag and add sugar.","(4) Then put a tea bag in a cup."],"k":1,"e":"[best order] 2 – 4 – 1 – 3 — boil → tea bag in the cup → pour water → take out the bag.","h":"رتّب خطوات إعداد الشاي."},{"n":2,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["2 – 4 – 3 – 1","2 – 3 – 4 – 1","3 – 2 – 4 – 1","2 – 3 – 1 – 4"],"x":["(1) When he woke up, the sun was shining.","(2) Last Friday, Badr went camping with his family.","(3) They put up the tent and made a fire.","(4) After dinner, they slept under the stars."],"k":1,"e":"[best order] 2 – 3 – 4 – 1 — introduction → tent and fire → slept → woke up.","h":"ابدأ بالجملة التي تذكر الاسم والزمن."},{"n":3,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["2 – 1 – 4 – 3","2 – 4 – 1 – 3","1 – 2 – 4 – 3","2 – 1 – 3 – 4"],"x":["(1) Before breakfast, I take a shower.","(2) My alarm rings at six o'clock.","(3) After breakfast, I brush my teeth and leave.","(4) Then I have breakfast with my family."],"k":0,"e":"[best order] 2 – 1 – 4 – 3 — alarm → shower before breakfast → breakfast → after breakfast.","h":"رتّب أحداث الصباح."},{"n":4,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["2 – 4 – 3 – 1","2 – 3 – 4 – 1","2 – 1 – 3 – 4","3 – 2 – 4 – 1"],"x":["(1) Soon, a small green plant appears.","(2) First, put some soil in a pot.","(3) Then plant a bean seed and water it.","(4) Put the pot near a sunny window."],"k":1,"e":"[best order] 2 – 3 – 4 – 1 — soil → seed → sunny window → the plant appears.","h":"رتّب خطوات الزراعة."},{"n":5,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["2 – 3 – 1 – 4","2 – 1 – 3 – 4","3 – 2 – 1 – 4","2 – 3 – 4 – 1"],"x":["(1) After that, we went to a restaurant for dinner.","(2) Yesterday, I went shopping with my brother.","(3) First, we bought new shoes for school.","(4) In the end, we came home very tired."],"k":0,"e":"[best order] 2 – 3 – 1 – 4 — Yesterday → First → After that → In the end.","h":"رتّب حسب كلمات التسلسل."},{"n":6,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["3 – 2 – 1 – 5 – 4","1 – 3 – 2 – 5 – 4","3 – 1 – 5 – 2 – 4","3 – 1 – 2 – 5 – 4"],"x":["(1) Next, wash the vegetables carefully.","(2) Then cut them into small pieces.","(3) First, buy fresh vegetables from the market.","(4) Finally, serve the salad with lemon juice.","(5) After that, mix them in a large bowl."],"k":3,"e":"[best order] 3 – 1 – 2 – 5 – 4 — First → Next → Then → After that → Finally.","h":"خمس خطوات بكلمات التسلسل."},{"n":7,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["2 – 1 – 4 – 3","4 – 2 – 1 – 3","2 – 1 – 3 – 4","2 – 4 – 1 – 3"],"x":["(1) In 2015, he moved to Riyadh to study at university.","(2) My uncle was born in a small village in 1997.","(3) After he graduated, he got a job as an engineer.","(4) As a child, he loved building things."],"k":3,"e":"[best order] 2 – 4 – 1 – 3 — born → as a child → university → after graduating.","h":"رتّب مراحل حياة العم."},{"n":8,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["3 – 4 – 1 – 2","1 – 3 – 4 – 2","3 – 1 – 4 – 2","3 – 1 – 2 – 4"],"x":["(1) Next, take it to the desk.","(2) Finally, return it within two weeks.","(3) To borrow a book, first find it on the shelf.","(4) Then the librarian will stamp it."],"k":2,"e":"[best order] 3 – 1 – 4 – 2 — find the book → desk → stamp → return.","h":"رتّب خطوات استعارة الكتاب."},{"n":9,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["2 – 4 – 1 – 3","1 – 2 – 4 – 3","4 – 2 – 1 – 3","2 – 1 – 4 – 3"],"x":["(1) Suddenly, dark clouds covered the sky.","(2) It was a sunny afternoon, and we were playing in the park.","(3) We ran home, but we were already wet.","(4) A few minutes later, heavy rain began to fall."],"k":3,"e":"[best order] 2 – 1 – 4 – 3 — sunny afternoon → Suddenly, clouds → A few minutes later, rain → ran home wet.","h":"ابدأ بوصف الموقف ثم التغيّر."},{"n":10,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["4 – 2 – 1 – 5 – 3","2 – 4 – 5 – 1 – 3","2 – 4 – 1 – 5 – 3","2 – 1 – 4 – 5 – 3"],"x":["(1) Rub your hands together for twenty seconds.","(2) Wet your hands with clean water.","(3) Dry them with a clean towel.","(4) Put some soap on your hands.","(5) Rinse the soap off with water."],"k":2,"e":"[best order] 2 – 4 – 1 – 5 – 3 — wet → soap → rub → rinse → dry.","h":"رتّب خطوات غسل اليدين منطقيًا."},{"n":11,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["2 – 5 – 3 – 1 – 4","2 – 3 – 5 – 1 – 4","3 – 2 – 5 – 1 – 4","2 – 3 – 1 – 5 – 4"],"x":["(1) Wait for ten minutes and watch what happens.","(2) First, fill a glass with warm water.","(3) Then add two spoons of salt and stir.","(4) Finally, write down your results.","(5) Next, put an egg gently into the water."],"k":1,"e":"[best order] 2 – 3 – 5 – 1 – 4 — First → Then salt → Next egg → wait → Finally results.","h":"رتّب خطوات التجربة."},{"n":12,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["3 – 2 – 4 – 1","4 – 3 – 2 – 1","3 – 4 – 1 – 2","3 – 4 – 2 – 1"],"x":["(1) The next morning, we visited the old tombs at Hegra.","(2) In the evening, we drove to our hotel.","(3) Last winter, my family took a trip to AlUla.","(4) We arrived at the airport in the afternoon."],"k":3,"e":"[best order] 3 – 4 – 2 – 1 — Last winter → afternoon → evening → next morning.","h":"اتبع عبارات الزمن."},{"n":13,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["4 – 2 – 1 – 3","2 – 1 – 4 – 3","2 – 4 – 3 – 1","2 – 4 – 1 – 3"],"x":["(1) After that, write your first draft.","(2) Before you start, read the question carefully.","(3) Finally, check your spelling and grammar.","(4) Next, make a short plan of your ideas."],"k":3,"e":"[best order] 2 – 4 – 1 – 3 — read → plan → draft → check.","h":"خطوات كتابة المقال."},{"n":14,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["First","Finally","After that","In the end"],"x":["______, mix the flour and the sugar. Then add the eggs."],"k":0,"e":"[transition / connector] First — The step before Then must start the process: First.","h":"الخطوة الأولى تحتاج First."},{"n":15,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["First","After that","Before","At first"],"x":["We played football for two hours. ______, we went home and had dinner."],"k":1,"e":"[transition / connector] After that — Going home comes later than the football: After that.","h":"الحدث اللاحق يحتاج After that."},{"n":16,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["before","after","then","first"],"x":["Turn off the lights ______ you leave the room."],"k":0,"e":"[transition / connector] before — Turning off the lights must happen earlier than leaving.","h":"إطفاء الأنوار قبل الخروج."},{"n":17,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["first","before","then","at first"],"x":["I did my homework, and ______ I watched television."],"k":2,"e":"[transition / connector] then — Watching TV comes after the homework: then.","h":"الحدث التالي يحتاج then."},{"n":18,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["First","Next","Finally","Before"],"x":["The journey was long and tiring. ______, after eight hours, we arrived in Madinah."],"k":2,"e":"[transition / connector] Finally — Arriving after eight hours is the end of the journey.","h":"نهاية الرحلة تحتاج Finally."},{"n":19,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["After","Then","First","Finally"],"x":["______ I finished school, I went to my grandmother's house."],"k":0,"e":"[transition / connector] After — After + a full clause shows the first action.","h":"After يأتي بعدها جملة كاملة."},{"n":20,"s":"(A) First, open the box. (B) Finally, take out the parts. (C) Then read the instructions. (D) Finally, build the model.","o":["First","Finally","Then","Finally"],"k":1,"e":"[error] Finally — Finally cannot be the second step; it should be Next.","h":"Finally لا تأتي في الخطوة الثانية."}]},{"l":["Part B — Mixed STEP Composition Analysis (Questions 21–30)","الجزء الثاني: أسئلة متنوعة من قسم تحليل الكتابة في اختبار STEP."],"q":[{"n":21,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 3","Sentence 4","Sentence 5","Sentence 6"],"x":["(1) Making Arabic coffee takes some time. (2) First, you roast the coffee beans. (3) Coffee is also popular in Turkey. (4) Then you grind them and boil them with water. (5) After that, you add cardamom. (6) Finally, you serve it in small cups."],"k":0,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 3 — The paragraph explains the steps; coffee in Turkey is off the process.","h":"القهوة في تركيا خارج الخطوات."},{"n":22,"s":"Which sentence is the best topic sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Mice are small animals.","Some people are afraid of cats.","Cats are good hunters.","Night is dark."],"x":["______ They can see well at night. They have soft feet, so they walk silently. They also have sharp claws for catching mice."],"k":2,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis] Cats are good hunters. — The details explain why cats hunt well.","h":"التفاصيل تشرح مهارة القطط في الصيد."},{"n":23,"s":"When (A) we (B) arrived, the film (C) has already (D) started.","o":["we","arrived","has","started"],"k":2,"e":"[error] has — The film started before we arrived in the past: had already started.","h":"الماضي التام had started."},{"n":24,"s":"Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Water is expensive.","I hope our trees will grow tall and strong.","My father works in an office.","Gardens need sunlight."],"x":["Last week, I helped my father plant trees in our garden. We dug holes and put the young trees in them. Then we watered them carefully. Now we water them every evening. ______"],"k":1,"e":"[concluding sentence] I hope our trees will grow tall and strong. — The closing sentence gives a hope about the trees.","h":"الخاتمة أمل يخص الأشجار."},{"n":25,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["so","because","or","but"],"x":["I wanted to buy the shoes, ______ they were too expensive."],"k":3,"e":"[transition / connector] but — wanted / too expensive is a contrast.","h":"التضاد يحتاج but."},{"n":26,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["The school has three floors.","My old school was small.","Friends are important.","Then a boy called Saeed asked me to sit with him."],"x":["My first day at the new school was difficult. I didn't know anyone. ______ By the end of the day, I had two new friends."],"k":3,"e":"[complete the paragraph] Then a boy called Saeed asked me to sit with him. — The gap explains how the day changed from difficult to friendly.","h":"الجملة تشرح تغيّر اليوم."},{"n":27,"s":"Which sentence is correct?","o":["We live here for five years.","We have lived here since five years.","We have lived here for five years.","We are living here for five years ago."],"k":2,"e":"[error] We have lived here for five years. — Present perfect + for + a period of time.","h":"المضارع التام مع for."},{"n":28,"s":"Which sentence would be the best topic sentence for a paragraph that explains how to prepare for an exam?","o":["Exams are usually in June.","Good exam preparation can be done in a few simple steps.","My brother failed his maths exam.","Some students like exams."],"k":1,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis] Good exam preparation can be done in a few simple steps. — It introduces a step-by-step paragraph about preparation.","h":"تقدم فقرة خطوات الاستعداد."},{"n":29,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 2","Sentence 3","Sentence 4","Sentence 5"],"x":["(1) Our new neighbours moved in last week. (2) They have three young children. (3) The father is a doctor at the hospital. (4) My mother took them a plate of sweets. (5) Hospitals need more nurses."],"k":3,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 5 — The need for nurses is off the topic of the new neighbours.","h":"حاجة المستشفيات خارج الموضوع."},{"n":30,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["so","but","or","although"],"x":["It started to rain, ______ we went inside."],"k":0,"e":"[transition / connector] so — Going inside is the result of the rain.","h":"النتيجة تحتاج so."}]}],"n":30},{"id":"2.4","t":"Writing Emails and Messages","html":"<p><strong>Unit 2 · Lesson 2.4 · CEFR A2 · STEP link: Composition Analysis (10%)</strong></p>\n<h3>Objectives</h3>\n<p>1. Write short emails and messages with the right greeting and closing.</p>\n<p>2. Choose words that suit the reader.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الأهداف</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">١. أن يكتب الطالب رسائل بريد إلكتروني ورسائل قصيرة بالتحية والختام المناسبين.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٢. أن يختار الكلمات التي تناسب القارئ.</span></p>\n<h3>The Skill</h3>\n<p>Every email has a clear structure: a GREETING (Dear Mr. Saad, / Hi Fahad,), an OPENING that says why you are writing (I am writing to ask about …), the MAIN MESSAGE with your questions or information, and a CLOSING (Thank you for your help. / Best regards, / See you soon,) followed by your name. Emails to teachers also need a clear subject line, for example: Question about the science project.</p>\n<p>The words you choose depend on the READER. To a teacher, a principal or someone you do not know, use a polite, formal style: Dear …, I would like to …, Could you please …?, I would be grateful if …, Best regards. To a friend or a family member, use a friendly, informal style: Hi …, Thanks!, Can you …?, See you soon. Never use texting language (u, wanna, gonna) in a formal email.</p>\n<p>Polite requests are very important. Compare: 'Send me the timetable.' (rude) with 'Could you please send me the timetable?' (polite). In STEP, word-choice items ask you to choose the most suitable greeting, closing or sentence for a reader and a situation. Complete-the-text items remove a sentence from an email; the correct sentence matches the purpose of the email and the sentences around it.</p>\n<p><strong>Examples:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>formal</strong> Dear Ms. Noura, · I am writing to ask about … · Best regards, Lama</p>\n<p><strong>informal</strong> Hi Fahad, · Thanks for the present! · See you soon, Omar</p>\n<p><strong>polite</strong> Could you please explain the homework again?</p>\n<p><strong>polite</strong> I would be grateful if you could check my essay.</p>\n<p><strong>✗ → ✓</strong> Tell me the date of the test. → Could you please tell me the date of the test?</p>\n<p><strong>✗ → ✓</strong> Hey teacher, I wanna join the club. → Dear Mr. Fahd, I would like to join the club.</p>\n<p><strong>✗ → ✓</strong> Subject: Hello → Subject: Question about the science project</p>\n<p><strong>✗ too formal</strong> Dear Sir, I humbly request the page numbers. (to a classmate)</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">المهارة</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">للبريد الإلكتروني بنية واضحة: تحية، ثم افتتاح يذكر سبب الكتابة، ثم الرسالة الرئيسة، ثم ختام واسم، مع عنوان واضح للرسالة. وتختار الكلمات حسب القارئ: أسلوب رسمي مهذب للمعلم والمدير ومن لا تعرفه (Dear, I would like to, Could you please, Best regards)، وأسلوب ودي غير رسمي للأصدقاء (Hi, Thanks, See you soon). ولا تستخدم لغة الرسائل النصية مثل u وwanna في البريد الرسمي.</span></p>\n<h3>Strategy</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>1. Ask: Who is the reader? A teacher (formal) or a friend (informal)?</p>\n<p>2. Ask: What is the purpose? To ask, to thank, to invite, to apologize or to cancel?</p>\n<p>3. For requests to adults, choose Could you please … / Would it be possible … / I would be grateful if …</p>\n<p>4. Reject options that are rude, too short, too informal for a teacher, or too formal for a friend.</p>\n<p>5. In complete-the-text items, choose the sentence that explains the purpose or links to the next question.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">اسأل: من القارئ؟ وما الغرض؟ واختر للطلب من الكبار عبارات مثل Could you please، وارفض البدائل الوقحة أو المختصرة جدًا أو غير الرسمية مع المعلم أو الرسمية جدًا مع الصديق، واختر في إكمال الرسالة الجملة التي تشرح الغرض أو ترتبط بالسؤال التالي.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Traps and Common Mistakes</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>✗ An informal greeting or closing in a formal email (Hey!, Bye!!!).</p>\n<p>✗ A very formal sentence in a message to a friend.</p>\n<p>✗ A request that sounds like an order (Send me …).</p>\n<p>✗ A sentence that is polite but does not match the purpose of the email.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Worked STEP Examples (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>Example 1. You are writing to a teacher you don't know well. Which greeting is the most suitable?</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. Hey Ahmed! B. Hi there,</p>\n<p>C. Yo, D. Dear Dr. Ahmed,</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The reader is a teacher you don't know well: formal.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> A formal greeting uses Dear + title + name.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> 'Dear Dr. Ahmed,' is the only formal option.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Answer: D</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الرسالة الرسمية تبدأ بـ Dear مع اللقب والاسم.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 2. Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Dear Ms. Reem, ______ Could you please send me the reading list for next term? Thank you, Jana</p>\n<p>A. I am a new student in your Grade 9 English class.</p>\n<p>B. Reading is fun.</p>\n<p>C. I have two sisters.</p>\n<p>D. Next term starts in January, I think.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The gap is the opening of the email, before the request.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The writer should introduce herself so the teacher knows who she is.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> 'I am a new student in your Grade 9 English class' does this.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Answer: A</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الجملة الافتتاحية تعرّف بالكاتبة وتربطها بالطلب.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 3. Which sentence is the most suitable in an email to a teacher?</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. Check my essay, OK?</p>\n<p>B. U should check my essay.</p>\n<p>C. I would be grateful if you could check my essay.</p>\n<p>D. Look at my essay now.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The reader is a teacher: the request must be polite.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> 'Check my essay, OK?' and 'Look at my essay now' sound like orders; 'U should' is texting language.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> 'I would be grateful if you could …' is polite and formal.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Answer: C</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">اختر الطلب المهذب الرسمي وارفض الأوامر ولغة الرسائل النصية.</span></p>\n<h3>Writing Task W-A2-04 — An email to a teacher asking about a project</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>Task:</strong> Write an email of 60–90 words to your teacher asking about a project. Use a suitable greeting, a clear purpose, two polite questions and a suitable closing.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">اكتب رسالة بريد إلكتروني من ستين إلى تسعين كلمة إلى معلمك تسأله فيها عن مشروع، واستخدم تحية مناسبة وغرضًا واضحًا وسؤالين مهذبين وختامًا مناسبًا.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Planning frame</strong></p>\n<p>1. Greeting: Dear Mr. / Ms. …,</p>\n<p>2. Opening: I am writing to ask about …</p>\n<p>3. Background: what you want to do in the project.</p>\n<p>4. Question 1: Could you please …?</p>\n<p>5. Question 2: Also, could you …?</p>\n<p>6. Closing: Thank you for your help. Best regards, name and class.</p>\n<p><strong>Model answer (71 words; target 60–90)</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Dear Mr. Saad, I hope you are well. I am writing to ask about the science project on renewable energy. I would like to make a model of a solar panel, but I am not sure if that is allowed. Could you please tell me if a model is acceptable? Also, could you tell me the deadline for the project? Thank you for your help. Best regards, Yasser Al-Ghamdi, Class 8A</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Examiner's commentary</strong></p>\n<p>▸ The greeting and closing are formal and suitable for a teacher.</p>\n<p>▸ The opening sentence states the purpose clearly.</p>\n<p>▸ Both questions use polite forms (Could you please …?).</p>\n<p>▸ The writer gives his full name and class so the teacher knows who he is.</p>\n<p><strong>Self-check before you hand in</strong></p>\n<p>☐ Is my greeting suitable for a teacher?</p>\n<p>☐ Did I say why I am writing in the first sentences?</p>\n<p>☐ Are my questions polite (Could you please …?)?</p>\n<p>☐ Did I avoid texting language (u, wanna, OK?)?</p>\n<p>☐ Did I finish with a thank-you, a closing and my name?</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">تأكد من التحية والختام الرسميين، ومن ذكر الغرض بوضوح، ومن صياغة الأسئلة بأدب، وتجنب لغة الرسائل النصية.</span></p>","wu":"Worked examples: Example 1 D · Example 2 A · Example 3 C","quiz":[{"l":["Answer all 30 questions. Read each paragraph or sentence carefully and choose the best answer (A, B, C or D).","أجب عن الأسئلة الثلاثين جميعها. اقرأ كل فقرة أو جملة بعناية واختر الإجابة الصحيحة من بين البدائل الأربعة.","Part A — Lesson Focus (Questions 1–20)","الجزء الأول: أسئلة على مهارة الدرس."],"q":[{"n":1,"s":"You are writing an email to your school principal. Which greeting is the most suitable?","o":["Hi buddy,","Hey!","Dear friend,","Dear Mr. Al-Harbi,"],"k":3,"e":"[word choice / register] Dear Mr. Al-Harbi, — A principal needs a formal greeting with a title and name.","h":"المدير يحتاج تحية رسمية."},{"n":2,"s":"Which closing is best for a short email to a friend?","o":["Yours faithfully, Ali","See you soon, Ali","Respectfully submitted, Ali","To whom it may concern, Ali"],"k":1,"e":"[word choice / register] See you soon, Ali — A friend gets a friendly closing; the others are very formal.","h":"الصديق يناسبه ختام ودي."},{"n":3,"s":"Which sentence is the most polite way to ask your teacher for help?","o":["Explain the homework again.","You must explain the homework.","I want you explain again.","Could you please explain the homework again?"],"k":3,"e":"[word choice / register] Could you please explain the homework again? — Could you please … is a polite request.","h":"Could you please طلب مهذب."},{"n":4,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["I love English very much.","My sister is in Grade 5.","The weather was cold yesterday.","I am writing about yesterday's English lesson."],"x":["Dear Ms. Noura, ______ I was sick and could not come to school. Could you tell me what homework I missed? Thank you, Lama"],"k":3,"e":"[complete the paragraph] I am writing about yesterday's English lesson. — The opening states the purpose: the missed lesson.","h":"الافتتاح يذكر الغرض."},{"n":5,"s":"Your friend sent you a message: 'Can you come to my house on Friday?' Which reply is the most suitable?","o":["No.","Sorry, I can't. I'm visiting my grandparents. Maybe next week?","Friday is the fifth day of the week.","Your house is big."],"k":1,"e":"[word choice / register] Sorry, I can't. I'm visiting my grandparents. Maybe next week? — A friendly refusal gives a reason and offers another time.","h":"رفض ودي مع سبب واقتراح."},{"n":6,"s":"Which subject line is best for an email asking your teacher about the science project?","o":["Question about the science project","Hello","Important!!!","Me"],"k":0,"e":"[word choice / register] Question about the science project — A subject line should say clearly what the email is about.","h":"العنوان يوضح موضوع الرسالة."},{"n":7,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["My birthday was in May last year.","Presents are expensive.","The watch is really nice.","I have a lot of homework."],"x":["Hi Fahad, Thanks for the birthday present! ______ I wear it every day. See you at school, Omar"],"k":2,"e":"[complete the paragraph] The watch is really nice. — 'I wear it' needs a sentence that names the present.","h":"الضمير it يحتاج مرجعًا."},{"n":8,"s":"Which sentence is the most formal?","o":["I wanna ask about the trip.","What's up with the trip?","Tell me about the trip, OK?","I would like to ask about the school trip."],"k":3,"e":"[word choice / register] I would like to ask about the school trip. — I would like to … is formal.","h":"I would like to عبارة رسمية."},{"n":9,"s":"You want to thank your teacher in an email. Which sentence is best?","o":["Thanks, mate!","Your help was OK.","Thank you very much for your help with my project.","Thank you for nothing."],"k":2,"e":"[word choice / register] Thank you very much for your help with my project. — It is polite and says what the thanks is for.","h":"شكر مهذب ومحدد."},{"n":10,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["I missed the announcement because I was at the dentist.","Maths is my favourite subject.","My dentist is very kind.","Class 7B has thirty students."],"x":["Dear Mr. Khalid, I am in Class 7B. ______ Could you please tell me the date of the next maths test? Best regards, Ziyad"],"k":0,"e":"[complete the paragraph] I missed the announcement because I was at the dentist. — The gap explains why the student needs to ask.","h":"الجملة تشرح سبب السؤال."},{"n":11,"s":"Which is the best way to end an email to a teacher?","o":["Best regards, Sultan","Bye!!!","Love, Sultan","Later, Sultan"],"k":0,"e":"[word choice / register] Best regards, Sultan — Best regards is a polite, formal closing.","h":"Best regards ختام رسمي."},{"n":12,"s":"Which sentence is the best way to invite a friend in a message?","o":["You will play football on Saturday.","Play football Saturday.","Would you like to play football with us on Saturday?","I order you to play football on Saturday."],"k":2,"e":"[word choice / register] Would you like to play football with us on Saturday? — Would you like to …? is a friendly invitation.","h":"Would you like to دعوة ودية."},{"n":13,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["Phones are useful.","My call was very short.","Dinner is my favourite meal.","I was helping my mother in the kitchen."],"x":["Hi Sara, I'm sorry I missed your call. ______ I'll call you back after dinner. Mona"],"k":3,"e":"[complete the paragraph] I was helping my mother in the kitchen. — The gap explains why the call was missed.","h":"الجملة تشرح سبب عدم الرد."},{"n":14,"s":"You need to cancel a meeting with your teacher. Which sentence is the most suitable?","o":["I am sorry, but I cannot come to our meeting on Monday.","I'm not coming. Bye.","Monday is bad, forget it.","No meeting for me."],"k":0,"e":"[word choice / register] I am sorry, but I cannot come to our meeting on Monday. — It apologizes politely and gives the information.","h":"اعتذار مهذب مع المعلومة."},{"n":15,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["so","or","but","because"],"x":["I would like to join the art club, ______ I am not sure about the times. Could you send me the timetable?"],"k":2,"e":"[transition / connector] but — wanting to join / not sure about the times is a contrast.","h":"التضاد يحتاج but."},{"n":16,"s":"Which request is the most polite?","o":["Would it be possible to borrow your notes?","Give me your notes.","I need your notes now.","Your notes, please, quickly."],"k":0,"e":"[word choice / register] Would it be possible to borrow your notes? — Would it be possible … is very polite.","h":"Would it be possible طلب مهذب جدًا."},{"n":17,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["I have played football for four years, and I would love to join the team.","Football is the most popular sport in the world.","My brother plays basketball.","The school field is very big."],"x":["Dear Mr. Fahd, My name is Rakan, and I am in Grade 8. I am writing to ask about the school's football team. ______ Could you tell me when the next try-out is? Thank you for your time. Yours sincerely, Rakan Al-Otaibi"],"k":0,"e":"[complete the paragraph] I have played football for four years, and I would love to join the team. — The gap gives background for the request to join.","h":"الجملة خلفية للطلب."},{"n":18,"s":"Which phrase is the best way to start a reply to an email?","o":["Why did you write?","Your email was long.","I got it.","Thank you for your email."],"k":3,"e":"[word choice / register] Thank you for your email. — Thanking the writer is a polite opening for a reply.","h":"شكر المرسل افتتاح مهذب للرد."},{"n":19,"s":"Which message is the most suitable to send to a classmate about homework?","o":["Pages?","Hi Nasser, do you know which pages we need to read for tomorrow?","Tell me the pages now.","Dear Sir, I humbly request the page numbers."],"k":1,"e":"[word choice / register] Hi Nasser, do you know which pages we need to read for tomorrow? — A friendly, clear question suits a classmate; the last is far too formal.","h":"سؤال ودي واضح يناسب الزميل."},{"n":20,"s":"Dear Ms. Huda, (A) I am writing to (B) ask about the project. (C) Could you (D) telling me the deadline?","o":["I am writing","ask","Could","telling"],"k":3,"e":"[error] telling — Could you is followed by the base verb: tell.","h":"بعد Could you يأتي الفعل المجرد."}]},{"l":["Part B — Mixed STEP Composition Analysis (Questions 21–30)","الجزء الثاني: أسئلة متنوعة من قسم تحليل الكتابة في اختبار STEP."],"q":[{"n":21,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["2 – 3 – 1 – 4","3 – 2 – 1 – 4","2 – 1 – 3 – 4","2 – 3 – 4 – 1"],"x":["(1) Could you tell me what time it starts?","(2) Dear Mr. Saleh,","(3) I am writing about the school concert next week.","(4) Thank you, Bader"],"k":0,"e":"[best order] 2 – 3 – 1 – 4 — greeting → purpose → question → closing.","h":"تحية ثم غرض ثم سؤال ثم ختام."},{"n":22,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 2","Sentence 3","Sentence 4","Sentence 5"],"x":["(1) My best friend Talal is moving to Canada. (2) His father got a new job there. (3) They will leave next month. (4) My mother bought a new oven. (5) I will miss him very much. (6) We promised to talk online every week."],"k":2,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 4 — The new oven is off the topic of the friend moving.","h":"الفرن خارج الموضوع."},{"n":23,"s":"Which sentence is the best topic sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Food is cheap in many places.","The new cinema in our city is excellent.","I watched a film with my brother.","Screens are getting bigger."],"x":["______ It has comfortable seats and big screens. The food is fresh and cheap. The staff are always friendly."],"k":1,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis] The new cinema in our city is excellent. — The details describe a good cinema.","h":"التفاصيل تصف السينما."},{"n":24,"s":"My (A) parents (B) was (C) very happy with (D) my results.","o":["parents","was","very","my"],"k":1,"e":"[error] was — parents is plural: were.","h":"الجمع يحتاج were."},{"n":25,"s":"Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Abha is in the south.","Honey is good for colds.","It was one of the best holidays we have ever had.","Summer is very hot in Riyadh."],"x":["My family went to Abha last summer. The weather was cool and rainy. We visited the mountains and the old villages. We also bought honey from a farm. ______"],"k":2,"e":"[concluding sentence] It was one of the best holidays we have ever had. — The closing sentence evaluates the whole holiday.","h":"الخاتمة تقييم للعطلة."},{"n":26,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["so","but","or","because"],"x":["I'm sorry I'm late. My bus broke down, ______ I had to walk."],"k":0,"e":"[transition / connector] so — Walking is the result of the broken bus.","h":"النتيجة تحتاج so."},{"n":27,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["3 – 1 – 2 – 4","3 – 2 – 1 – 4","2 – 3 – 1 – 4","1 – 3 – 2 – 4"],"x":["(1) to my teacher","(2) an email","(3) I sent","(4) last night"],"k":1,"e":"[best order] 3 – 2 – 1 – 4 — I sent an email to my teacher last night.","h":"فاعل وفعل ثم مفعول ثم إلى من ثم زمن."},{"n":28,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["Maths was invented long ago.","My maths teacher is from Egypt.","Some students like art more.","However, there are ways to make it easier."],"x":["Many students find maths difficult. ______ For example, they can practise a little every day and ask questions in class."],"k":3,"e":"[complete the paragraph] However, there are ways to make it easier. — 'For example, they can practise' needs a sentence about ways to improve.","h":"المثال يحتاج جملة عن طرق التسهيل."},{"n":29,"s":"(A) If it (B) will rain tomorrow, (C) we will (D) stay at home.","o":["If","will rain","we","stay"],"k":1,"e":"[error] will rain — After if, we use the present simple: If it rains.","h":"بعد if نستخدم المضارع البسيط."},{"n":30,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 4","Sentence 5","Sentence 6","Sentence 7"],"x":["(1) Our school is planning a charity day. (2) Students will sell cakes and drinks. (3) There will also be games for children. (4) All the money will go to a children's hospital. (5) Parents are welcome to come. (6) My cousin's school has a new swimming pool. (7) We hope to raise ten thousand riyals."],"k":2,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 6 — The cousin's swimming pool is off the topic of the charity day.","h":"المسبح خارج موضوع يوم الخير."}]}],"n":30},{"id":"2.5","t":"Fragments and Run-on Sentences","html":"<p><strong>Unit 2 · Lesson 2.5 · CEFR A2 · STEP link: Composition Analysis (10%)</strong></p>\n<h3>Objectives</h3>\n<p>1. Identify sentence fragments and run-on sentences.</p>\n<p>2. Choose the correctly punctuated version.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الأهداف</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">١. أن يتعرف الطالب على أشباه الجمل الناقصة والجمل المتصلة الخاطئة.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٢. أن يختار الصياغة الصحيحة الترقيم.</span></p>\n<h3>The Skill</h3>\n<p>A FRAGMENT is part of a sentence that is written as if it were a full sentence. It is missing a subject, a verb or a main idea. Examples: 'Bought a new car last week.' (no subject) · 'A beautiful old house near the sea.' (no verb) · 'Because the weather was cool.' (no main idea: Because … what happened?). Fix a fragment by adding what is missing or by joining it to the sentence before or after it.</p>\n<p>A RUN-ON sentence joins two complete sentences without the right punctuation or connector. 'The test was easy everyone passed it.' (no punctuation) and 'The film was boring, we left early.' (only a comma — this is called a comma splice) are both run-ons. Fix a run-on in one of three ways: (1) use a full stop: The test was easy. Everyone passed it. (2) use a comma + and / but / so: The film was boring, so we left early. (3) use because / although / when: Because the film was boring, we left early.</p>\n<p>Words like because, when, after, although, if and which start a part that cannot stand alone. 'After we finished our lunch.' is a fragment; 'After we finished our lunch, we went home.' is complete. Also note: although and but do not go together (Although it was cold, but … is wrong). In STEP, these items ask: Which is a complete sentence? Which is written correctly? Which is the best way to correct this sentence?</p>\n<p><strong>Examples:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>✗ fragment</strong> Running across the playground. → ✓ He was running across the playground.</p>\n<p><strong>✗ fragment</strong> Because I was tired. → ✓ I went to bed early because I was tired.</p>\n<p><strong>✗ fragment</strong> I bought a new bag. Which was expensive. → ✓ I bought a new bag, which was expensive.</p>\n<p><strong>✗ run-on</strong> I love reading my favourite book is about space. → ✓ I love reading. My favourite book is about space.</p>\n<p><strong>✗ comma splice</strong> It was raining, we stayed at home. → ✓ It was raining, so we stayed at home.</p>\n<p><strong>✗ run-on</strong> My phone was broken I couldn't call you. → ✓ Because my phone was broken, I couldn't call you.</p>\n<p><strong>✗ → ✓</strong> Although it was cold, but we went out. → Although it was cold, we went out.</p>\n<p><strong>✓</strong> When the bell rang, the students went to class.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">المهارة</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">شبه الجملة الناقص جزء من جملة يُكتب كأنه جملة كاملة، وينقصه الفاعل أو الفعل أو الفكرة الرئيسة مثل Because the weather was cool. أما الجملة المتصلة الخاطئة فتربط جملتين كاملتين دون ترقيم أو أداة ربط، أو بفاصلة فقط. وتصحح بنقطة، أو بفاصلة مع and أو but أو so، أو بـ because أو although أو when. ولا تجتمع although مع but.</span></p>\n<h3>Strategy</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>1. For every option, find the subject and the main verb.</p>\n<p>2. If a group of words starts with because, when, after, although or which and has nothing else, it is a fragment.</p>\n<p>3. Count the complete ideas: two complete ideas need a full stop or a comma + connector.</p>\n<p>4. A comma alone between two complete sentences is wrong (comma splice).</p>\n<p>5. Check that although and but are not used together.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">ابحث في كل بديل عن الفاعل والفعل الرئيس، واعلم أن العبارة التي تبدأ بـ because أو when أو although وحدها ناقصة، وعدّ الأفكار الكاملة: الفكرتان تحتاجان نقطة أو فاصلة مع أداة ربط، والفاصلة وحدها بين جملتين خطأ، ولا تجمع although مع but.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Traps and Common Mistakes</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>✗ A long group of words that looks like a sentence but has no main verb.</p>\n<p>✗ Two sentences joined with only a comma.</p>\n<p>✗ A full stop that separates a because-part from its main idea.</p>\n<p>✗ although and but used together in one sentence.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Worked STEP Examples (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>Example 1. Which group of words is a complete sentence?</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. The children played in the garden.</p>\n<p>B. Playing in the garden.</p>\n<p>C. The children in the garden.</p>\n<p>D. While the children played in the garden.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> One distractor has no subject; another has no verb.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> 'While the children played …' needs a main idea after it.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Only 'The children played in the garden.' is complete.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Answer: A</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الجملة الكاملة فيها فاعل وفعل وفكرة تامة.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 2. Which is the best way to correct this run-on sentence: 'I was hungry I made a sandwich.'?</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. I was hungry, I made a sandwich.</p>\n<p>B. I was hungry I made, a sandwich.</p>\n<p>C. I was hungry, so I made a sandwich.</p>\n<p>D. I was. Hungry I made a sandwich.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> There are two complete ideas: I was hungry / I made a sandwich.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> A comma alone is a comma splice; the other options break the sentence wrongly.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> A comma + so is correct.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Answer: C</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الفاصلة وحدها لا تكفي، والصحيح فاصلة مع so.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 3. Which of these contains a sentence fragment?</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. We visited Abha because the weather was cool.</p>\n<p>B. We visited Abha. Because the weather was cool.</p>\n<p>C. The weather was cool, so we visited Abha.</p>\n<p>D. We visited Abha. The weather was cool.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Look for a part that starts with because, when or which and stands alone.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> 'Because the weather was cool.' is separated by a full stop.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> That option contains a fragment.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Answer: B</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">العبارة المفصولة بنقطة والتي تبدأ بـ Because ناقصة.</span></p>\n<h3>Writing Task W-A2-05 — A day trip to a mountain village</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>Task:</strong> Write 60–90 words about a day trip to a mountain village (real or imagined). Use full stops and connectors correctly so that there are no fragments or run-on sentences.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">اكتب من ستين إلى تسعين كلمة عن رحلة يوم واحد إلى قرية جبلية (حقيقية أو متخيلة)، واستخدم النقاط وأدوات الربط بشكل صحيح دون جمل ناقصة أو متصلة خاطئة.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Planning frame</strong></p>\n<p>1. When and where did you go, and with whom?</p>\n<p>2. How did you travel, and why did you leave early or late?</p>\n<p>3. What did the village look like?</p>\n<p>4. What did you do in the morning and at lunchtime?</p>\n<p>5. How did the day end?</p>\n<p>6. Closing sentence: your feeling about the trip.</p>\n<p><strong>Model answer (84 words; target 60–90)</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Last spring, my family took a day trip to Rijal Almaa, a village in the mountains near Abha. We left early in the morning because the road was long. The village has tall stone houses with colourful windows. We visited a small museum, and a guide told us about the history of the village. At lunchtime, we ate fresh bread with honey. In the afternoon, it became cloudy, so we drove back home. It was a short trip, but I will never forget it.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Examiner's commentary</strong></p>\n<p>▸ Every sentence has a subject, a verb and a complete idea.</p>\n<p>▸ Two ideas are joined correctly with because, and, so and but.</p>\n<p>▸ Commas come before and, so and but when they join two sentences.</p>\n<p>▸ Time expressions (Last spring, At lunchtime, In the afternoon) organize the trip in order.</p>\n<p><strong>Self-check before you hand in</strong></p>\n<p>☐ Does every sentence have a subject and a main verb?</p>\n<p>☐ Did I join two complete ideas with a full stop or with a comma + connector?</p>\n<p>☐ Is any part that starts with because or when joined to a main idea?</p>\n<p>☐ Did I avoid using although and but together?</p>\n<p>☐ Is my paragraph 60–90 words?</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">راجع كل جملة: هل فيها فاعل وفعل؟ هل ربطت الفكرتين بنقطة أو بفاصلة مع أداة ربط؟ هل العبارات التي تبدأ بـ because مرتبطة بفكرة رئيسة؟</span></p>","wu":"Worked examples: Example 1 A · Example 2 C · Example 3 B","quiz":[{"l":["Answer all 30 questions. Read each paragraph or sentence carefully and choose the best answer (A, B, C or D).","أجب عن الأسئلة الثلاثين جميعها. اقرأ كل فقرة أو جملة بعناية واختر الإجابة الصحيحة من بين البدائل الأربعة.","Part A — Lesson Focus (Questions 1–20)","الجزء الأول: أسئلة على مهارة الدرس."],"q":[{"n":1,"s":"Which group of words is a complete sentence?","o":["Bought a new car last week.","My uncle's new car from last week.","My uncle bought a new car last week.","Because my uncle bought a new car."],"k":2,"e":"[error] My uncle bought a new car last week. — Subject (My uncle) + verb (bought) + complete idea.","h":"فاعل وفعل وفكرة تامة."},{"n":2,"s":"Which of these is a sentence fragment?","o":["We finished our lunch.","After lunch, we went home.","After we finished our lunch.","We went home after we finished our lunch."],"k":2,"e":"[error] After we finished our lunch. — 'After we finished our lunch.' has no main idea.","h":"تنقصها الفكرة الرئيسة."},{"n":3,"s":"Which is written correctly?","o":["It was raining we stayed at home.","It was raining, we stayed at home.","It was raining so, we stayed at home.","It was raining, so we stayed at home."],"k":3,"e":"[error] It was raining, so we stayed at home. — Comma + so joins the two complete ideas.","h":"فاصلة مع so."},{"n":4,"s":"Which is the best way to correct this run-on sentence: 'I love reading my favourite book is about space.'?","o":["I love reading, my favourite book is about space.","I love reading. My favourite book is about space.","I love reading my favourite. Book is about space.","I love. Reading my favourite book is about space."],"k":1,"e":"[error] I love reading. My favourite book is about space. — A full stop separates the two complete ideas.","h":"نقطة تفصل الفكرتين."},{"n":5,"s":"Which group of words is NOT a complete sentence?","o":["He ran across the playground.","His friends ran with him.","They were playing a game.","Running across the playground with his friends."],"k":3,"e":"[error] Running across the playground with his friends. — It has no subject and no main verb.","h":"بلا فاعل وفعل رئيس."},{"n":6,"s":"Which is written correctly?","o":["My sister is a doctor. She works at King Fahd Hospital.","My sister is a doctor she works at King Fahd Hospital.","My sister is a doctor, she works at King Fahd Hospital.","My sister is a doctor. Works at King Fahd Hospital."],"k":0,"e":"[error] My sister is a doctor. She works at King Fahd Hospital. — Two complete sentences separated by a full stop.","h":"جملتان كاملتان بينهما نقطة."},{"n":7,"s":"Which is the best way to complete the fragment 'When the bell rang.'?","o":["When the bell rang. The students.","When the bell rang and loud.","When the bell rang, the students went to class.","When the bell, the students went to class."],"k":2,"e":"[error] When the bell rang, the students went to class. — A main idea is added after the when-part.","h":"أضفنا الفكرة الرئيسة."},{"n":8,"s":"Which is written correctly?","o":["We were tired we finished the work.","We were tired, but we finished the work.","We were tired, we finished the work.","We were tired. But finished the work."],"k":1,"e":"[error] We were tired, but we finished the work. — Comma + but joins two complete, contrasting ideas.","h":"فاصلة مع but."},{"n":9,"s":"Which of these is a sentence fragment?","o":["We live in an old house.","A beautiful old house near the sea.","The house is near the sea.","It is beautiful."],"k":1,"e":"[error] A beautiful old house near the sea. — It has no verb.","h":"بلا فعل."},{"n":10,"s":"Which is the best way to correct this sentence: 'The film was boring, we left early.'?","o":["The film was boring we left early.","The film was boring, we left, early.","The film was boring, so we left early.","The film. Was boring, we left early."],"k":2,"e":"[error] The film was boring, so we left early. — The comma splice is fixed with so.","h":"نصحح الفاصلة الخاطئة بـ so."},{"n":11,"s":"Which group of words is a complete sentence?","o":["Because of the heavy rain, the match was cancelled.","Because of the heavy rain.","The heavy rain and the cancelled match.","Because the match was cancelled because of the rain."],"k":0,"e":"[error] Because of the heavy rain, the match was cancelled. — It has a main idea: the match was cancelled.","h":"فيها فكرة رئيسة."},{"n":12,"s":"Which is written correctly?","o":["I called Hamad, and he answered immediately.","I called Hamad he answered immediately.","I called Hamad, he answered immediately.","I called Hamad. And answered immediately."],"k":0,"e":"[error] I called Hamad, and he answered immediately. — Comma + and joins the two complete ideas.","h":"فاصلة مع and."},{"n":13,"s":"Which of these is a run-on sentence?","o":["The test was easy, so everyone passed it.","Everyone passed the test.","Because the test was easy, everyone passed it.","The test was easy everyone passed it."],"k":3,"e":"[error] The test was easy everyone passed it. — Two complete ideas with no punctuation or connector.","h":"فكرتان بلا ترقيم أو أداة ربط."},{"n":14,"s":"Which is the best way to correct the fragment 'For example, apples and bananas.'?","o":["For example, apples and bananas are.","I eat a lot of fruit, for example, apples and bananas.","For example. Apples and bananas.","Apples, for example, and bananas."],"k":1,"e":"[error] I eat a lot of fruit, for example, apples and bananas. — The example is joined to a full sentence with a subject and a verb.","h":"المثال مرتبط بجملة كاملة."},{"n":15,"s":"Which is written correctly?","o":["My brother, who lives in Jeddah, is an engineer.","My brother who lives in Jeddah. Is an engineer.","My brother lives in Jeddah, is an engineer.","My brother, who lives in Jeddah."],"k":0,"e":"[error] My brother, who lives in Jeddah, is an engineer. — The who-part sits inside a full sentence: My brother … is an engineer.","h":"الجملة الرئيسة My brother is an engineer."},{"n":16,"s":"Which group of words is a complete sentence?","o":["To get good marks.","To get good marks, you need to study every day.","Studying every day to get good marks.","If you want to get good marks."],"k":1,"e":"[error] To get good marks, you need to study every day. — Subject (you) + verb (need) + complete idea.","h":"فاعل وفعل وفكرة تامة."},{"n":17,"s":"Which is the best way to join these sentences: 'The shop was closed. We went to another one.'?","o":["The shop was closed we went to another one.","The shop was closed, we went to another one.","The shop was closed, because we went to another one.","The shop was closed, so we went to another one."],"k":3,"e":"[error] The shop was closed, so we went to another one. — Going to another shop is the result: comma + so.","h":"النتيجة مع so."},{"n":18,"s":"Which of these contains a sentence fragment?","o":["I bought a new bag. Which was very expensive.","I bought a new bag, which was very expensive.","I bought a new bag. It was very expensive.","The new bag that I bought was very expensive."],"k":0,"e":"[error] I bought a new bag. Which was very expensive. — 'Which was very expensive.' cannot stand alone.","h":"العبارة التي تبدأ بـ Which لا تقف وحدها."},{"n":19,"s":"Which is written correctly?","o":["Although it was cold. We went to the beach.","Although it was cold, but we went to the beach.","Although it was cold, we went to the beach.","It was cold we went to the beach although."],"k":2,"e":"[error] Although it was cold, we went to the beach. — although-part + comma + main idea, with no but.","h":"although دون but."},{"n":20,"s":"Which is the best way to correct this run-on sentence: 'My phone was broken I couldn't call you I'm sorry.'?","o":["My phone was broken, so I couldn't call you. I'm sorry.","My phone was broken, I couldn't call you, I'm sorry.","My phone was broken I couldn't call you. I'm sorry.","My phone. Was broken so I couldn't call you I'm sorry."],"k":0,"e":"[error] My phone was broken, so I couldn't call you. I'm sorry. — so joins cause and result; a full stop separates the apology.","h":"so للنتيجة ونقطة قبل الاعتذار."}]},{"l":["Part B — Mixed STEP Composition Analysis (Questions 21–30)","الجزء الثاني: أسئلة متنوعة من قسم تحليل الكتابة في اختبار STEP."],"q":[{"n":21,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 2","Sentence 3","Sentence 4","Sentence 5"],"x":["(1) Mountain villages in the south are very beautiful. (2) The houses are made of stone. (3) The desert is very hot in summer. (4) Farmers grow fruit on terraces. (5) The air is fresh and cool. (6) Many tourists visit them every year."],"k":1,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 3 — The hot desert is off the topic of mountain villages.","h":"الصحراء خارج موضوع القرى الجبلية."},{"n":22,"s":"Which sentence is the best topic sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Watches are not expensive.","A smart watch can do many useful things.","My heart rate is normal.","I walk ten thousand steps a day."],"x":["______ It shows the time and counts your steps. It can also measure your heart rate. You can even answer calls with it."],"k":1,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis] A smart watch can do many useful things. — The details are uses of a smart watch.","h":"التفاصيل استخدامات الساعة الذكية."},{"n":23,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["2 – 1 – 3 – 4","3 – 2 – 1 – 4","2 – 3 – 4 – 1","2 – 3 – 1 – 4"],"x":["(1) We reached the top after two hours.","(2) Early in the morning, we started climbing the mountain.","(3) The path was steep and rocky.","(4) The view from the top was amazing."],"k":3,"e":"[best order] 2 – 3 – 1 – 4 — start → the path → reached the top → the view.","h":"رتّب أحداث الصعود."},{"n":24,"s":"Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Paper comes from trees.","The programme has already made a big difference.","Thursday is the last school day.","Plastic bins are blue."],"x":["Our school started a recycling programme this year. There are special bins for paper and plastic in every classroom. Students collect the bins every Thursday. Last month, we recycled more than two hundred kilograms of paper. ______"],"k":1,"e":"[concluding sentence] The programme has already made a big difference. — The closing sentence evaluates the programme.","h":"الخاتمة تقييم للبرنامج."},{"n":25,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["but","or","so","because"],"x":["The road was closed, ______ we took a different route."],"k":2,"e":"[transition / connector] so — Taking a different route is the result.","h":"النتيجة تحتاج so."},{"n":26,"s":"(A) Each of the (B) students (C) have (D) a laptop.","o":["Each","students","have","a"],"k":2,"e":"[error] have — Each is singular: has.","h":"Each مفرد فنستخدم has."},{"n":27,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["At lunchtime, a farmer invited us to eat with his family.","The fields are green in spring.","Farmers wake up early.","Sunsets are red and orange."],"x":["Our trip to the village was wonderful. In the morning, we walked through the fields. ______ In the evening, we watched the sunset from a hill."],"k":0,"e":"[complete the paragraph] At lunchtime, a farmer invited us to eat with his family. — The gap needs the middle of the day, between morning and evening.","h":"الفراغ يحتاج حدث منتصف اليوم."},{"n":28,"s":"Which sentence is the most suitable for a message to your teacher?","o":["Check my answers.","U check my answers, ok?","Could you please check my answers when you have time?","Hurry up and check my answers."],"k":2,"e":"[word choice / register] Could you please check my answers when you have time? — It is a polite request suitable for a teacher.","h":"طلب مهذب يناسب المعلم."},{"n":29,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 1","Sentence 2","Sentence 3","Sentence 4"],"x":["(1) The Arabian oryx is a beautiful white animal. (2) It once almost disappeared from the wild. (3) Scientists protected it in special reserves. (4) Zebras have black and white stripes. (5) Today, there are thousands of oryx again."],"k":3,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 4 — Zebras are off the topic of the Arabian oryx.","h":"الحمار الوحشي خارج الموضوع."},{"n":30,"s":"My father (A) has (B) worked at the bank (C) since (D) ten years.","o":["has","worked","since","ten years"],"k":3,"e":"[error] ten years — since needs a starting point; a period needs for: for ten years.","h":"المدة تحتاج for."}]}],"n":30},{"id":"2.6","t":"Concluding Sentences","html":"<p><strong>Unit 2 · Lesson 2.6 · CEFR A2 · STEP link: Composition Analysis (10%)</strong></p>\n<h3>Objectives</h3>\n<p>1. Write a concluding sentence that restates the main idea.</p>\n<p>2. Choose the best concluding sentence.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الأهداف</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">١. أن يكتب الطالب جملة ختامية تعيد صياغة الفكرة الرئيسة.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٢. أن يختار أفضل جملة ختامية.</span></p>\n<h3>The Skill</h3>\n<p>The concluding sentence is the LAST sentence of a paragraph. It tells the reader that the paragraph is finished. A good concluding sentence does one or more of these jobs: it RESTATES the main idea in new words, it SUMMARIZES the supporting points, or it gives a final THOUGHT, opinion, advice or hope about the topic.</p>\n<p>Concluding sentences often begin with a signal: In conclusion, … / To sum up, … / In short, … / All in all, … / For these reasons, … / That is why … / Clearly, … They should NOT introduce a brand-new idea, give one more small detail, or move to a different topic. For example, after a paragraph about a trip to the zoo, 'Next week, we are going to the museum' is a new topic, not a conclusion.</p>\n<p>In STEP, concluding-sentence items show a paragraph with a blank at the end. To choose the answer, first identify the topic sentence and the main idea. Then choose the option that brings the reader back to that idea. Wrong options are usually (1) a new detail, (2) a related fact that is true but does not conclude, or (3) a new topic.</p>\n<p><strong>Examples:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>restate</strong> For these reasons, more students should walk to school.</p>\n<p><strong>summary</strong> Healthy food, exercise and sleep are the keys to a healthy life.</p>\n<p><strong>opinion</strong> Al-Balad is an important part of Saudi history.</p>\n<p><strong>advice</strong> Parents should therefore watch how their children use the internet.</p>\n<p><strong>hope</strong> I hope our trees will grow tall and strong.</p>\n<p><strong>✗ new topic</strong> Next week, we are going to the museum. (after a paragraph about the zoo)</p>\n<p><strong>✗ new detail</strong> Lions are dangerous animals. (one more fact, not a conclusion)</p>\n<p><strong>signals</strong> In conclusion · To sum up · In short · All in all · That is why · Clearly</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">المهارة</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الجملة الختامية آخر جملة في الفقرة، وتخبر القارئ بانتهائها، فتعيد صياغة الفكرة الرئيسة أو تلخص النقاط الداعمة أو تقدم فكرة أخيرة كرأي أو نصيحة أو أمل. وتبدأ غالبًا بعبارات مثل In conclusion وTo sum up وThat is why، ولا يجوز أن تأتي بفكرة جديدة أو تفصيلة صغيرة أو موضوع آخر.</span></p>\n<h3>Strategy</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>1. Read the first sentence and write the main idea in a few words.</p>\n<p>2. Read the supporting sentences to see what they prove.</p>\n<p>3. Choose the option that returns to the main idea or gives a final opinion, advice or hope about it.</p>\n<p>4. Reject options that add one more detail, a related fact, or a new topic.</p>\n<p>5. Read the paragraph with your answer: it should sound finished.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">اقرأ الجملة الأولى وحدد الفكرة الرئيسة، ثم اقرأ الجمل الداعمة، واختر البديل الذي يعود إلى الفكرة الرئيسة أو يقدم رأيًا أو نصيحة أو أملًا، وارفض التفصيلة الإضافية والحقيقة الجانبية والموضوع الجديد.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Traps and Common Mistakes</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>✗ One more supporting detail at the end.</p>\n<p>✗ A true fact related to a word in the paragraph.</p>\n<p>✗ A sentence that starts a new topic or a plan for the future.</p>\n<p>✗ A concluding signal (In conclusion) used with an idea that is not the main idea.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Worked STEP Examples (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>Example 1. Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Riding a bicycle is a great hobby. It keeps you fit. It is cheap, and it does not pollute the air. You can also explore new places with friends. ______</p>\n<p>A. Bicycles were invented in Europe.</p>\n<p>B. Air pollution is a big problem.</p>\n<p>C. Everyone should try cycling as a hobby.</p>\n<p>D. My friend has a red bicycle.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Main idea: riding a bicycle is a great hobby.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Supporting points: fitness, cheap, clean, exploring.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Only 'Everyone should try cycling as a hobby' returns to the main idea.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Answer: C</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">اختر الجملة التي تعود إلى الفكرة الرئيسة.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 2. Which word or phrase best fills the blank?</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>______, healthy food, exercise and sleep are the keys to a healthy life.</p>\n<p>A. For example B. In short</p>\n<p>C. Firstly D. On the other hand</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The sentence lists three ideas together: a summary.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Summaries begin with In short, To sum up or In conclusion.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> For example, Firstly and On the other hand do not conclude.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Answer: B</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">عبارة In short للتلخيص.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 3. Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Our trip to the zoo was fantastic. We saw lions, giraffes and elephants. We fed the goats in the children's area. We even had a picnic near the lake. ______</p>\n<p>A. Next week, we are going to the museum.</p>\n<p>B. Lions are dangerous animals.</p>\n<p>C. Goats eat grass and leaves.</p>\n<p>D. It was a day that none of us will forget.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Main idea: the zoo trip was fantastic.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> 'Next week …' is a new topic; the facts about lions and goats are extra details.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> 'It was a day that none of us will forget' concludes the paragraph.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Answer: D</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">ارفض الموضوع الجديد والتفاصيل الإضافية.</span></p>\n<h3>Writing Task W-A2-06 — A healthy habit I want to keep</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>Task:</strong> Write 60–90 words about a healthy habit you want to keep. End with a clear concluding sentence that restates your main idea or gives a final thought.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">اكتب من ستين إلى تسعين كلمة عن عادة صحية تريد المحافظة عليها، واختم بجملة ختامية واضحة تعيد الفكرة الرئيسة أو تقدم فكرة أخيرة.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Planning frame</strong></p>\n<p>1. Topic sentence: One healthy habit I want to keep is …</p>\n<p>2. Background: what was the problem before?</p>\n<p>3. What did you change, and how?</p>\n<p>4. Details: how often, how much, instead of what?</p>\n<p>5. Result: how do you feel now?</p>\n<p>6. Concluding sentence: restate the habit and its value.</p>\n<p><strong>Model answer (84 words; target 60–90)</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>One healthy habit I want to keep is drinking more water. Last year, I often felt tired and had headaches in the afternoon. My doctor told me that I was not drinking enough water. Now I carry a bottle to school and drink about eight glasses every day. I also drink water instead of fizzy drinks. As a result, I feel more active and my headaches have stopped. Drinking water is a simple habit, but it has made a big difference to my health.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Examiner's commentary</strong></p>\n<p>▸ The topic sentence names the habit clearly.</p>\n<p>▸ The supporting sentences tell a short story: problem → change → result.</p>\n<p>▸ As a result shows the effect of the new habit.</p>\n<p>▸ The concluding sentence restates the habit and gives a final thought about its value.</p>\n<p><strong>Self-check before you hand in</strong></p>\n<p>☐ Does my topic sentence name the habit?</p>\n<p>☐ Did I explain why I started and what changed?</p>\n<p>☐ Does my last sentence return to the main idea?</p>\n<p>☐ Did I avoid adding a new idea in the last sentence?</p>\n<p>☐ Is my paragraph 60–90 words?</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">تأكد من أن الجملة الأخيرة تعود إلى الفكرة الرئيسة ولا تضيف فكرة جديدة.</span></p>","wu":"Worked examples: Example 1 C · Example 2 B · Example 3 D","quiz":[{"l":["Answer all 30 questions. Read each paragraph or sentence carefully and choose the best answer (A, B, C or D).","أجب عن الأسئلة الثلاثين جميعها. اقرأ كل فقرة أو جملة بعناية واختر الإجابة الصحيحة من بين البدائل الأربعة.","Part A — Lesson Focus (Questions 1–20)","الجزء الأول: أسئلة على مهارة الدرس."],"q":[{"n":1,"s":"Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?","o":["My school is two kilometres away.","For these reasons, more students should walk to school.","Petrol is cheap in Saudi Arabia.","Some students ride bicycles."],"x":["Walking to school has many benefits. It is good exercise. It saves money on petrol. It is also better for the environment than driving. ______"],"k":1,"e":"[concluding sentence] For these reasons, more students should walk to school. — The conclusion summarizes the benefits and gives advice.","h":"الخاتمة تلخص الفوائد وتنصح."},{"n":2,"s":"Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Cardamom is an expensive spice.","My grandmother is seventy years old.","I feel happy and safe whenever I am in that kitchen.","Wooden tables are heavy."],"x":["My grandmother's kitchen is my favourite room in her house. It always smells of fresh bread and cardamom. There is a big wooden table where we eat together. My grandmother tells us stories while she cooks. ______"],"k":2,"e":"[concluding sentence] I feel happy and safe whenever I am in that kitchen. — The conclusion returns to the kitchen with a feeling.","h":"الخاتمة تعود إلى المطبخ مع شعور."},{"n":3,"s":"Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Fast food is popular with teenagers.","My mother cooks very well.","Some kitchens are very small.","Every young person should learn to cook a few simple dishes."],"x":["Learning to cook is a useful skill for young people. They can prepare healthy meals for themselves. They can save money because they do not need to buy fast food. They can also help their families at home. ______"],"k":3,"e":"[concluding sentence] Every young person should learn to cook a few simple dishes. — The conclusion gives advice based on the main idea.","h":"الخاتمة نصيحة مبنية على الفكرة."},{"n":4,"s":"Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Trees need water to grow.","Twenty is an even number.","We have maths every morning.","We are proud that our school is becoming greener."],"x":["Last week, our class planted twenty trees around the school. Each student was responsible for one tree. We dug the holes, planted the trees and watered them. Now we check them every morning. ______"],"k":3,"e":"[concluding sentence] We are proud that our school is becoming greener. — The conclusion gives a feeling about the whole project.","h":"الخاتمة شعور تجاه المشروع."},{"n":5,"s":"Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?","o":["That is why it is important to be on time.","Some lessons start at seven.","Teachers write information on the board.","Many people work in offices."],"x":["Being late can cause many problems. Late students miss important information at the beginning of lessons. They also disturb other students when they come in. In the future, being late can cause problems at work. ______"],"k":0,"e":"[concluding sentence] That is why it is important to be on time. — That is why … restates the main idea as advice.","h":"That is why تعيد الفكرة نصيحةً."},{"n":6,"s":"Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Camel races are popular today.","Tents are made of many materials.","Milk is white.","Without camels, life in the desert would have been very difficult."],"x":["Camels have helped people in Arabia for thousands of years. They carried people and goods across the desert. Their milk was an important food. Their hair was used to make tents and clothes. ______"],"k":3,"e":"[concluding sentence] Without camels, life in the desert would have been very difficult. — The conclusion shows how important camels were.","h":"الخاتمة تبين أهمية الجمال."},{"n":7,"s":"Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?","o":["I will always be thankful for his patience.","Bicycles have two wheels.","My brother is studying at university.","Many children fall off bicycles."],"x":["My older brother taught me how to ride a bicycle. At first, I fell many times. He held the back of the bike and ran next to me. After two weeks, I could ride alone. ______"],"k":0,"e":"[concluding sentence] I will always be thankful for his patience. — The conclusion gives a final feeling about the brother's help.","h":"الخاتمة شعور تجاه مساعدة الأخ."},{"n":8,"s":"Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Modern libraries are much more than places to borrow books.","Books are heavy to carry.","Cafés sell coffee and tea.","Children like activities."],"x":["Libraries are changing. In the past, people went to libraries only to borrow books. Today, libraries also offer computers, online courses and study rooms. Some even have cafés and spaces for children's activities. ______"],"k":0,"e":"[concluding sentence] Modern libraries are much more than places to borrow books. — The conclusion restates the idea of change.","h":"الخاتمة تعيد فكرة التغيير."},{"n":9,"s":"Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Gardens are beautiful in spring.","Teeth should be brushed twice a day.","Showers are better than baths.","If we change these small habits, we can save a lot of water."],"x":["Using too much water is a serious problem in many countries. People leave the tap running while they brush their teeth. Some water their gardens in the middle of the day, when the sun is very hot. Others take very long showers. ______"],"k":3,"e":"[concluding sentence] If we change these small habits, we can save a lot of water. — The conclusion offers a solution to the problem.","h":"الخاتمة تقدم حلًا."},{"n":10,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["For example","First of all","In conclusion","However"],"x":["______, playing sport is good for both the body and the mind."],"k":2,"e":"[transition / connector] In conclusion — The sentence restates a main idea, so it needs a concluding signal.","h":"إعادة الفكرة تحتاج عبارة ختامية."},{"n":11,"s":"Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?","o":["With a little effort, you will soon have many new friends.","Sports teams train after school.","Lunch is at twelve o'clock.","Some classmates are shy."],"x":["There are many ways to make new friends at a new school. You can join a club or a sports team. You can sit with different students at lunch. You can also offer to help classmates with their work. ______"],"k":0,"e":"[concluding sentence] With a little effort, you will soon have many new friends. — The conclusion returns to making friends with encouragement.","h":"الخاتمة تعود إلى تكوين الصداقات."},{"n":12,"s":"Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?","o":["That is why I always look forward to winter.","Summer is very hot in Riyadh.","Tea is popular in many countries.","Camping equipment is expensive."],"x":["My favourite season is winter. In winter, the weather in Riyadh is cool and pleasant. My family often goes camping in the desert. We sit around the fire and drink hot tea. ______"],"k":0,"e":"[concluding sentence] That is why I always look forward to winter. — The conclusion restates why winter is the favourite season.","h":"الخاتمة تعيد سبب حب الشتاء."},{"n":13,"s":"Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?","o":["The internet was invented in the twentieth century.","Parents should therefore watch how their children use the internet.","Some websites are very fast.","Screens are getting cheaper."],"x":["The internet can be dangerous for children. Some websites show violent or unsuitable things. Strangers may try to talk to children online. Children may also spend too many hours in front of screens. ______"],"k":1,"e":"[concluding sentence] Parents should therefore watch how their children use the internet. — The conclusion gives advice that follows from the dangers.","h":"الخاتمة نصيحة نتيجة للمخاطر."},{"n":14,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["To sum up","For instance","Next","Because"],"x":["______, there are three main reasons why I enjoy learning English."],"k":0,"e":"[transition / connector] To sum up — The sentence summarizes the reasons, so it needs To sum up.","h":"التلخيص يحتاج To sum up."},{"n":15,"s":"Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Coral lives in the sea.","UNESCO has offices in Paris.","Al-Balad is an important part of Saudi history.","Wood is used to make furniture."],"x":["Old Jeddah, called Al-Balad, is a special place. Its houses are hundreds of years old. They are made of coral stone and have beautiful wooden windows. In 2014, it became a UNESCO World Heritage Site. ______"],"k":2,"e":"[concluding sentence] Al-Balad is an important part of Saudi history. — The conclusion restates the importance of Al-Balad.","h":"الخاتمة تعيد أهمية البلد."},{"n":16,"s":"Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Many video games are expensive.","History is my favourite subject.","So, not all video games are bad, if we choose them carefully.","Some players play all night."],"x":["Some people think that video games are a waste of time. However, some games can be useful. Strategy games help players think and plan. Some games teach history or languages. ______"],"k":2,"e":"[concluding sentence] So, not all video games are bad, if we choose them carefully. — The conclusion answers the opening opinion with the paragraph's view.","h":"الخاتمة ترد على الرأي في البداية."},{"n":17,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["For example","All in all","Firstly","Instead"],"x":["We will have a great time at the camp. ______, I am sure everyone will enjoy it."],"k":1,"e":"[transition / connector] All in all — All in all introduces a final overall judgement.","h":"All in all للحكم النهائي."},{"n":18,"s":"Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Football is played in every country.","Motor racing is dangerous.","Stadiums can hold thousands of people.","Sport is clearly becoming a bigger part of life in Saudi Arabia."],"x":["Saudi Arabia is investing in sports. The country has hosted big events in football, tennis and motor racing. New stadiums and sports centres are being built in many cities. More young people are joining sports clubs than ever before. ______"],"k":3,"e":"[concluding sentence] Sport is clearly becoming a bigger part of life in Saudi Arabia. — The conclusion sums up all the evidence of growth.","h":"الخاتمة تلخص أدلة النمو."},{"n":19,"s":"Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Diaries can be bought in any bookshop.","Some people feel sad on Mondays.","Keeping a diary is a small habit with big benefits.","Writing skills are tested in exams."],"x":["Writing a diary has several advantages. It helps you remember special days. It improves your writing skills. It can also help you understand your feelings when you are sad or worried. ______"],"k":2,"e":"[concluding sentence] Keeping a diary is a small habit with big benefits. — The conclusion restates the advantages in new words.","h":"الخاتمة تعيد المزايا بكلمات جديدة."},{"n":20,"s":"Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Studies are done by scientists.","Unhealthy snacks are cheap.","Clearly, breakfast should not be skipped.","Some students play sports after school."],"x":["Many people believe that breakfast is not important, so they skip it. However, studies show that students who eat breakfast concentrate better in class. They also have more energy for sports. In addition, they are less likely to eat unhealthy snacks later. ______"],"k":2,"e":"[concluding sentence] Clearly, breakfast should not be skipped. — The conclusion answers the opening belief with the evidence.","h":"الخاتمة ترد على الاعتقاد بالدليل."}]},{"l":["Part B — Mixed STEP Composition Analysis (Questions 21–30)","الجزء الثاني: أسئلة متنوعة من قسم تحليل الكتابة في اختبار STEP."],"q":[{"n":21,"s":"Which sentence is the best topic sentence for the paragraph?","o":["The new metro is the best way to travel in Riyadh.","Taxis are expensive.","Riyadh is a big city.","Trains were invented long ago."],"x":["______ First, it is very fast. Second, it is comfortable and clean. Third, it is cheaper than taking a taxi."],"k":0,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis] The new metro is the best way to travel in Riyadh. — The reasons support a claim about the metro.","h":"الأسباب تدعم فكرة عن المترو."},{"n":22,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 2","Sentence 3","Sentence 4","Sentence 5"],"x":["(1) Olive oil is a healthy food. (2) It is good for the heart. (3) It contains vitamins. (4) People use it in salads and cooking. (5) Coconuts grow on tall trees. (6) Many doctors recommend it."],"k":3,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 5 — Coconuts are off the topic of olive oil.","h":"جوز الهند خارج موضوع زيت الزيتون."},{"n":23,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["2 – 4 – 3 – 1","2 – 3 – 4 – 1","3 – 2 – 4 – 1","2 – 3 – 1 – 4"],"x":["(1) As a result, she won a place at a top university.","(2) Last year, my cousin Nouf decided to study medicine.","(3) She studied for many hours every day.","(4) She also took extra classes in chemistry and biology."],"k":1,"e":"[best order] 2 – 3 – 4 – 1 — decision → studied → also extra classes → As a result.","h":"القرار ثم الجهد ثم النتيجة."},{"n":24,"s":"The (A) children (B) was playing (C) quietly in (D) the garden.","o":["children","was","quietly","the"],"k":1,"e":"[error] was — children is plural: were.","h":"الجمع يحتاج were."},{"n":25,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["Dates are grown in Al-Qassim.","The factory was very big.","I like chocolate more than dates.","Then we watched machines put them into boxes."],"x":["Our class visited a dates factory last month. First, we saw how the dates are washed. ______ Finally, we tasted different kinds of dates."],"k":3,"e":"[complete the paragraph] Then we watched machines put them into boxes. — The gap needs the middle step of the visit.","h":"الفراغ يحتاج خطوة وسطى."},{"n":26,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["so","because","but","or"],"x":["I studied hard for the test, ______ I still found it difficult."],"k":2,"e":"[transition / connector] but — studied hard / still difficult is a contrast.","h":"التضاد يحتاج but."},{"n":27,"s":"Which is the most suitable way to end an email to a teacher?","o":["That's all. Bye!","Thank you for your time. Best regards, Hamad","Answer quickly, Hamad","Whatever, Hamad"],"k":1,"e":"[word choice / register] Thank you for your time. Best regards, Hamad — A polite thank-you and a formal closing suit a teacher.","h":"شكر مهذب وختام رسمي."},{"n":28,"s":"Which is written correctly?","o":["We missed the bus we took a taxi.","We missed the bus, so we took a taxi.","We missed the bus, we took a taxi.","We missed the bus. So took a taxi."],"k":1,"e":"[error] We missed the bus, so we took a taxi. — Comma + so joins the two complete ideas.","h":"فاصلة مع so."},{"n":29,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["3 – 1 – 4 – 2","3 – 1 – 2 – 4","1 – 3 – 4 – 2","3 – 4 – 1 – 2"],"x":["(1) visit","(2) every summer","(3) We","(4) our cousins in Abha"],"k":0,"e":"[best order] 3 – 1 – 4 – 2 — We visit our cousins in Abha every summer.","h":"فاعل ثم فعل ثم مفعول ثم زمن."},{"n":30,"s":"(A) Everyone in my class (B) are (C) excited about (D) the trip.","o":["Everyone","are","excited","the"],"k":1,"e":"[error] are — Everyone is singular: is.","h":"Everyone مفرد فنستخدم is."}]}],"n":30}],"sc":{},"review":{"quiz":[{"l":["Unit Review — 50 questions covering all six lessons of the unit. Choose the best answer (A, B, C or D).","مراجعة الوحدة: خمسون سؤالًا تغطي دروس الوحدة الستة، اختر الإجابة الصحيحة."],"q":[{"n":1,"s":"Which sentence is the best topic sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Libraries have many books.","Some teachers are strict.","I really like my new school.","Clubs meet on Wednesdays."],"x":["______ It has a big playground and a new library. The teachers are kind and helpful. There are also many after-school clubs."],"k":2,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis · 2.1] I really like my new school. — The details are reasons to like the school.","h":"التفاصيل أسباب لحب المدرسة."},{"n":2,"s":"Which greeting is best for an email to your football coach?","o":["Yo Saleh!","Hey man,","Dear Coach Saleh,","To my football guy,"],"k":2,"e":"[word choice / register · 2.4] Dear Coach Saleh, — A coach is an adult in charge: a polite greeting with a title.","h":"المدرب يحتاج تحية مهذبة مع اللقب."},{"n":3,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["before","after","then","finally"],"x":["Wash the rice ______ you cook it."],"k":0,"e":"[transition / connector · 2.3] before — Washing comes earlier than cooking.","h":"الغسل قبل الطبخ."},{"n":4,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["Our city is very old.","They have trees, grass and play areas for children.","Some families stay at home.","Grass needs a lot of water."],"x":["Our city has many green parks. ______ Families go there in the evening to relax."],"k":1,"e":"[complete the paragraph · 2.2] They have trees, grass and play areas for children. — The gap describes the parks, which the next sentence talks about.","h":"الجملة تصف الحدائق."},{"n":5,"s":"Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?","o":["For Saudis, coffee is much more than a drink.","Coffee beans come from Yemen and Ethiopia.","Weddings are usually at night.","Some people prefer tea."],"x":["Saudi coffee is an important part of our culture. We serve it to guests to welcome them. It is always offered at weddings and Eid. Families drink it together every afternoon. ______"],"k":0,"e":"[concluding sentence · 2.6] For Saudis, coffee is much more than a drink. — The conclusion restates the cultural importance of coffee.","h":"الخاتمة تعيد الأهمية الثقافية للقهوة."},{"n":6,"s":"Which group of words is a complete sentence?","o":["Landed safely in Dammam.","The plane safely in Dammam.","The plane landed safely in Dammam.","When the plane landed in Dammam."],"k":2,"e":"[error · 2.5] The plane landed safely in Dammam. — Subject + verb + complete idea.","h":"فاعل وفعل وفكرة تامة."},{"n":7,"s":"Which sentence is the best topic sentence for a paragraph about the dangers of using a phone while driving?","o":["Phones have many apps.","Using a phone while driving is very dangerous.","My father drives a big car.","Some roads are very long."],"k":1,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis · 2.1] Using a phone while driving is very dangerous. — It names the topic and the controlling idea (dangerous).","h":"تذكر الموضوع والفكرة المسيطرة."},{"n":8,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["2 – 1 – 4 – 3","2 – 4 – 1 – 3","1 – 2 – 4 – 3","2 – 1 – 3 – 4"],"x":["(1) Then she put the books in her bag.","(2) Lama finished her homework at eight.","(3) Finally, she went to bed.","(4) After that, she prepared her clothes for the next day."],"k":0,"e":"[best order · 2.3] 2 – 1 – 4 – 3 — homework → Then books → After that clothes → Finally bed.","h":"اتبع كلمات التسلسل."},{"n":9,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["My project is about animals.","I saw that you have a book about the solar system.","Sunday is a school day.","Books are expensive."],"x":["Hi Reem, ______ Can I borrow it for my project? I'll give it back on Sunday. Thanks, Dana"],"k":1,"e":"[complete the paragraph · 2.4] I saw that you have a book about the solar system. — 'Can I borrow it' needs a sentence that names the thing.","h":"it تحتاج مرجعًا."},{"n":10,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 1","Sentence 2","Sentence 3","Sentence 4"],"x":["(1) Owls are interesting birds. (2) They hunt at night. (3) Parrots can learn to speak. (4) They can turn their heads almost all the way round. (5) Their soft feathers help them fly silently."],"k":2,"e":"[irrelevant sentence · 2.2] Sentence 3 — The paragraph is about owls; parrots are a different bird.","h":"الببغاوات خارج موضوع البوم."},{"n":11,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["For example","Firstly","Overall","Instead"],"x":["______, our trip to the museum was both fun and educational."],"k":2,"e":"[transition / connector · 2.6] Overall — Overall gives a final judgement.","h":"Overall للحكم العام."},{"n":12,"s":"Which is written correctly?","o":["The match ended late we got home at midnight.","The match ended late, we got home at midnight.","The match ended late. So got home at midnight.","The match ended late, so we got home at midnight."],"k":3,"e":"[error · 2.5] The match ended late, so we got home at midnight. — Comma + so joins the two complete ideas.","h":"فاصلة مع so."},{"n":13,"s":"Which sentence is the best topic sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Post offices offer many services.","Stamps are small and colourful.","Bills come every month.","My uncle sent me a parcel."],"x":["______ They deliver letters and parcels to homes. They also sell stamps. In some places, people can pay their bills there."],"k":0,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis · 2.1] Post offices offer many services. — The details are services of the post office.","h":"التفاصيل خدمات البريد."},{"n":14,"s":"Which is the most polite way to ask a shop assistant for help?","o":["Excuse me, could you help me find the shoes, please?","Where are the shoes?!","Shoes. Now.","You, show me the shoes."],"k":0,"e":"[word choice / register · 2.4] Excuse me, could you help me find the shoes, please? — Excuse me + could you … please is polite.","h":"Excuse me مع could you please طلب مهذب."},{"n":15,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["2 – 1 – 4 – 3","4 – 2 – 1 – 3","2 – 4 – 1 – 3","2 – 4 – 3 – 1"],"x":["(1) She called an ambulance immediately.","(2) Yesterday, a man fell in the street near our house.","(3) The ambulance arrived ten minutes later.","(4) My mother saw him from the window."],"k":2,"e":"[best order · 2.3] 2 – 4 – 1 – 3 — fell → mother saw him → called → arrived.","h":"رتّب الأحداث منطقيًا."},{"n":16,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["London is a big city.","He can also speak to customers from other countries.","Emails are fast.","My father works in Jeddah."],"x":["Learning English has helped my father in his job. He can read emails from foreign companies. ______ Last year, he even travelled to London for a meeting."],"k":1,"e":"[complete the paragraph · 2.2] He can also speak to customers from other countries. — The gap needs another way English helps him at work.","h":"طريقة أخرى تساعده بها الإنجليزية."},{"n":17,"s":"Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?","o":["She is an example for all of us.","Vegetables are cheap in the market.","Some children study at home.","Eighty years is a long time."],"x":["Our neighbour, Umm Khalid, is eighty years old, but she is very active. She walks for an hour every morning. She grows vegetables in her garden. She also teaches the Quran to children in the neighbourhood. ______"],"k":0,"e":"[concluding sentence · 2.6] She is an example for all of us. — The conclusion gives a final opinion about Umm Khalid.","h":"الخاتمة رأي نهائي."},{"n":18,"s":"Which of these is a sentence fragment?","o":["Since the beginning of the year.","The year began in January.","We have studied hard since January.","Since January, we have studied hard."],"k":0,"e":"[error · 2.5] Since the beginning of the year. — It has no subject or verb.","h":"بلا فاعل وفعل."},{"n":19,"s":"Which sentence is the best topic sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Roads need repairing.","My mother is a nurse.","Offices open at eight.","People do many different kinds of jobs."],"x":["______ Some help people who are sick. Others build houses and roads. Many work in offices and schools."],"k":3,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis · 2.1] People do many different kinds of jobs. — The details are different jobs.","h":"التفاصيل وظائف مختلفة."},{"n":20,"s":"You want to apologize to your teacher for missing a class. Which sentence is best?","o":["Sorry, whatever.","I am sorry that I missed your class on Tuesday.","I didn't come. So what?","Your class was on Tuesday."],"k":1,"e":"[word choice / register · 2.4] I am sorry that I missed your class on Tuesday. — A sincere, polite apology.","h":"اعتذار صادق مهذب."},{"n":21,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["At last","First","Before","Next to"],"x":["We waited for an hour. ______, the bus arrived."],"k":0,"e":"[transition / connector · 2.3] At last — At last shows the end of a long wait.","h":"At last بعد انتظار طويل."},{"n":22,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 1","Sentence 2","Sentence 3","Sentence 4"],"x":["(1) Our school's science lab is very modern. (2) The school bus is old and slow. (3) It has new microscopes and computers. (4) Students do experiments there every week. (5) There are safety rules on every wall. (6) It is my favourite room in the school."],"k":1,"e":"[irrelevant sentence · 2.2] Sentence 2 — The school bus is off the topic of the lab.","h":"الحافلة خارج موضوع المختبر."},{"n":23,"s":"Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Teenagers need to find a better balance between online and offline life.","Videos can be very funny.","Homework is important.","Sport keeps us healthy."],"x":["Many teenagers spend hours online every day. They chat with friends, watch videos and play games. Some forget to do their homework or go to bed late. Others stop doing sport. ______"],"k":0,"e":"[concluding sentence · 2.6] Teenagers need to find a better balance between online and offline life. — The conclusion gives advice based on the problems described.","h":"الخاتمة نصيحة مبنية على المشكلات."},{"n":24,"s":"Which is the best way to correct this run-on sentence: 'The museum was closed we went to the park instead.'?","o":["The museum was closed, so we went to the park instead.","The museum was closed, we went to the park instead.","The museum was closed we went, to the park instead.","The museum. Was closed we went to the park instead."],"k":0,"e":"[error · 2.5] The museum was closed, so we went to the park instead. — Comma + so fixes the run-on.","h":"فاصلة مع so تصحح الجملة."},{"n":25,"s":"Which sentence is the best topic sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Mud is found near rivers.","Saudi Arabia has many historic buildings.","Tourists take many photos.","Some buildings are very new."],"x":["______ Some of them are hundreds of years old. They were built from mud and stone. Today, many have been repaired so that tourists can visit them."],"k":1,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis · 2.1] Saudi Arabia has many historic buildings. — The details describe old buildings.","h":"التفاصيل عن المباني التاريخية."},{"n":26,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["The bus left at seven.","Science centres are in many cities.","Space is very big.","Everyone in our class enjoyed it very much."],"x":["Dear Mr. Majed, Thank you for organizing the school trip to the science centre. ______ I especially liked the space show. Best regards, Hussain"],"k":3,"e":"[complete the paragraph · 2.4] Everyone in our class enjoyed it very much. — The gap continues the thank-you message.","h":"الجملة تكمل رسالة الشكر."},{"n":27,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["2 – 4 – 1 – 5 – 3","1 – 2 – 4 – 5 – 3","2 – 1 – 5 – 4 – 3","2 – 1 – 4 – 5 – 3"],"x":["(1) Next, we chose a topic for our project.","(2) Our teacher put us into groups of four.","(3) Finally, we presented our work to the class.","(4) After that, each of us found information online.","(5) Then we put all the information on a poster."],"k":3,"e":"[best order · 2.3] 2 – 1 – 4 – 5 – 3 — groups → Next topic → After that research → Then poster → Finally presentation.","h":"خمس خطوات بالترتيب."},{"n":28,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["Snakes have no legs.","Farmers grow wheat and dates.","Only a small number of them are poisonous.","Some people keep cats."],"x":["Many people are afraid of snakes. However, most snakes are not dangerous. ______ In fact, snakes help farmers by eating mice."],"k":2,"e":"[complete the paragraph · 2.2] Only a small number of them are poisonous. — The gap supports the idea that most snakes are not dangerous.","h":"الجملة تدعم أن معظم الثعابين غير خطيرة."},{"n":29,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["For instance","However","Then","In short"],"x":["My new phone has a great camera, a big screen and a long battery life. ______, it is the best phone I have ever had."],"k":3,"e":"[transition / connector · 2.6] In short — In short introduces a summary of the points.","h":"In short للتلخيص."},{"n":30,"s":"Which is written correctly?","o":["Although the test was long, but I finished it on time.","Although the test was long, I finished it on time.","Although the test was long. I finished it on time.","The test was long I finished it on time."],"k":1,"e":"[error · 2.5] Although the test was long, I finished it on time. — although-part + comma + main idea, without but.","h":"although دون but."},{"n":31,"s":"Which sentence is the best topic sentence for a paragraph about why people enjoy camping in the desert?","o":["The desert is very large.","We camped last January.","There are several reasons why people enjoy camping in the desert.","Tents come in many colours."],"k":2,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis · 2.1] There are several reasons why people enjoy camping in the desert. — It introduces reasons for enjoying desert camping.","h":"تقدم أسباب حب التخييم."},{"n":32,"s":"Which sentence is the most suitable in a message to a close friend?","o":["Thanks for the gift! I love it!","I hereby express my gratitude for the gift.","Dear Sir, thank you for the gift.","The gift was received."],"k":0,"e":"[word choice / register · 2.4] Thanks for the gift! I love it! — A friend gets a warm, informal message.","h":"الصديق تناسبه رسالة ودية."},{"n":33,"s":"(A) First, we (B) visited the museum. (C) Finally, we had lunch. (D) In the end, we went home.","o":["First","visited","Finally","In the end"],"k":2,"e":"[error · 2.3] Finally — Finally cannot come before In the end; the middle step needs Then or After that.","h":"Finally لا تأتي قبل In the end."},{"n":34,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 4","Sentence 5","Sentence 6","Sentence 7"],"x":["(1) Exercise helps students in many ways. (2) It makes their bodies strong. (3) It reduces stress before exams. (4) It helps them sleep better. (5) Many students study in the library. (6) It can also help them make friends in a team. (7) Every student should exercise regularly."],"k":1,"e":"[irrelevant sentence · 2.2] Sentence 5 — Studying in the library is not a benefit of exercise.","h":"الدراسة في المكتبة ليست فائدة للرياضة."},{"n":35,"s":"Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Today, people use GPS.","Crops need water and sun.","Some stars are very bright.","The stars were an important guide for people in the past."],"x":["In the past, people in Arabia used the stars to find their way across the desert. They knew the position of each star at different times of the year. They also used the stars to know when to plant crops. Some of the star names we use today come from Arabic. ______"],"k":3,"e":"[concluding sentence · 2.6] The stars were an important guide for people in the past. — The conclusion restates the role of the stars.","h":"الخاتمة تعيد دور النجوم."},{"n":36,"s":"Which of these contains a sentence fragment?","o":["Fahad won the race even though he was tired.","Fahad won the race. Even though he was tired.","Even though he was tired, Fahad won the race.","Fahad was tired, but he won the race."],"k":1,"e":"[error · 2.5] Fahad won the race. Even though he was tired. — 'Even though he was tired.' cannot stand alone.","h":"العبارة لا تقف وحدها."},{"n":37,"s":"Which sentence is the best topic sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Buses are cheaper than cars.","Restaurants open at noon.","I like going to the mall.","Our city is busy all day long."],"x":["______ In the morning, the streets are full of cars and buses. At lunchtime, people crowd the restaurants. In the evening, the shopping malls are busy until midnight."],"k":3,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis · 2.1] Our city is busy all day long. — Morning, lunchtime and evening: busy all day.","h":"الصباح والظهر والمساء: مزدحمة طوال اليوم."},{"n":38,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["Thursday is my favourite day.","The dentist is very busy.","I have an appointment with the dentist at one o'clock.","I like my school very much."],"x":["Dear Ms. Asma, I am writing to ask for permission to leave school early on Thursday. ______ I will make sure to catch up on any work I miss. Yours sincerely, Ghada"],"k":2,"e":"[complete the paragraph · 2.4] I have an appointment with the dentist at one o'clock. — The gap gives the reason for the request.","h":"الجملة تذكر سبب الطلب."},{"n":39,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["2 – 3 – 4 – 1","4 – 2 – 3 – 1","2 – 4 – 3 – 1","2 – 4 – 1 – 3"],"x":["(1) Later that day, the doctor said he could go home.","(2) Last Monday, my grandfather felt sick.","(3) The doctor checked him and gave him some medicine.","(4) We took him to the hospital immediately."],"k":2,"e":"[best order · 2.3] 2 – 4 – 3 – 1 — felt sick → hospital → doctor checked → could go home.","h":"رتّب الأحداث زمنيًا."},{"n":40,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["Computers are expensive for some families.","Young children need a lot of sleep.","Some games are violent.","There are many educational programs designed especially for them."],"x":["Some people think that young children should not use computers. However, computers can help children learn in many ways. ______ For example, children can practise reading and maths with fun games."],"k":3,"e":"[complete the paragraph · 2.2] There are many educational programs designed especially for them. — The gap supports the positive view and leads into the example.","h":"الجملة تدعم الرأي الإيجابي وتمهد للمثال."},{"n":41,"s":"Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Secrets are hard to keep.","Friends like this are rare, so we should value them.","Some people have many friends online.","Trouble can happen to anyone."],"x":["A good friend is someone you can trust. A good friend listens to your problems and keeps your secrets. A good friend tells you the truth, even when it is difficult. A good friend also helps you when you are in trouble. ______"],"k":1,"e":"[concluding sentence · 2.6] Friends like this are rare, so we should value them. — The conclusion gives a final thought about good friends.","h":"الخاتمة فكرة نهائية عن الصديق."},{"n":42,"s":"Which is the best way to correct this sentence: 'I like history, my brother likes science.'?","o":["I like history my brother likes science.","I like history, my brother, likes science.","I like history. But likes science.","I like history, but my brother likes science."],"k":3,"e":"[error · 2.5] I like history, but my brother likes science. — Comma + but fixes the comma splice.","h":"فاصلة مع but."},{"n":43,"s":"Which sentence is the best topic sentence for the paragraph?","o":["National parks are valuable in many ways.","Hunting is popular in some countries.","Scientists study many subjects.","Some animals are rare."],"x":["______ Scientists can study animals in their natural homes. Tourists can enjoy the beautiful scenery. Most importantly, rare plants and animals are protected from hunting and building."],"k":0,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis · 2.1] National parks are valuable in many ways. — The details are values of national parks.","h":"التفاصيل فوائد المحميات."},{"n":44,"s":"Which sentence is the best way to start an email to someone you have never met?","o":["Hey, it's me!","Guess who this is!","You don't know me, LOL.","My name is Turki Al-Mutairi, and I am a student at Al-Andalus School."],"k":3,"e":"[word choice / register · 2.4] My name is Turki Al-Mutairi, and I am a student at Al-Andalus School. — A stranger needs a clear, polite introduction.","h":"الغريب يحتاج تعريفًا مهذبًا."},{"n":45,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["Before","First","As soon as","Finally"],"x":["______ the plane landed, the passengers turned on their phones."],"k":2,"e":"[transition / connector · 2.3] As soon as — Turning on phones happens immediately after landing.","h":"مباشرة بعد الهبوط."},{"n":46,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 3","Sentence 4","Sentence 5","Sentence 6"],"x":["(1) Our family's weekend routine is simple. (2) On Friday, we pray together at the mosque. (3) After lunch, we visit our grandparents. (4) On Saturday morning, we clean the house. (5) In the evening, we go for a walk by the sea. (6) Many restaurants are open late at night."],"k":3,"e":"[irrelevant sentence · 2.2] Sentence 6 — Restaurants opening late is not part of the family routine.","h":"المطاعم خارج روتين الأسرة."},{"n":47,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["For example","In the beginning","For all these reasons","On the other hand"],"x":["Reading improves your vocabulary, your writing and your imagination. ______, it is one of the most useful habits you can have."],"k":2,"e":"[transition / connector · 2.6] For all these reasons — The conclusion follows from the listed benefits.","h":"الخاتمة نتيجة للفوائد المذكورة."},{"n":48,"s":"Which is written correctly?","o":["When the rain stopped. The children went outside to play.","When the rain stopped, the children went outside to play.","The rain stopped the children went outside to play.","When the rain stopped, but the children went outside to play."],"k":1,"e":"[error · 2.5] When the rain stopped, the children went outside to play. — when-part + comma + main idea.","h":"when ثم فاصلة ثم الفكرة الرئيسة."},{"n":49,"s":"You are writing to a company to ask about a summer job. Which sentence is the most suitable?","o":["Got any summer jobs?","Give me a summer job, please.","I need money, so I want a job.","I would like to know whether you have any summer jobs for students."],"k":3,"e":"[word choice / register · 2.4] I would like to know whether you have any summer jobs for students. — A formal, polite enquiry suits a company.","h":"سؤال رسمي مهذب يناسب الشركة."},{"n":50,"s":"Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Teachers work very hard every day.","The internet is useful, but it cannot replace a good teacher.","The internet was not available fifty years ago.","Some students prefer online games."],"x":["Some students think that they can learn everything from the internet, so they do not need teachers. It is true that the internet has a lot of information. However, teachers can explain difficult ideas, answer questions and notice when a student is having problems. They also encourage students to keep trying. ______"],"k":1,"e":"[concluding sentence · 2.6] The internet is useful, but it cannot replace a good teacher. — The conclusion balances both sides and states the writer's view.","h":"الخاتمة توازن بين الجانبين وتذكر رأي الكاتب."}]}],"n":50}};
